{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil","id":1426997,"title":"When was the exact moment that the Technocratcy began to be written as less \"evil\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-02T10:10:07-08:00","id":1426997,"title":"When was the exact moment that the Technocratcy began to be written as less \"evil\"?","content":"That is, when the good they had done and their more positive traits were focused on. Also when did it become clear that the Traditions were being less than honest in their descriptions of the former?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T11:10:21-08:00","id":1427005,"title":"","content":"The Book of Shadows (the first edition's Player's Guide) started its Technocracy section with a vignette about an NWO agent trying to stop a CoX mage and his Hollower partners from distributing dangerous drugs and gunrunning in the local neighborhood. The section then went into some detail as to how one could play a Technocrat as a good guy, despite the organization as a whole being corrupt. (Reviewing the book, the vignette was actually split up over the various parts of the Technocracy section.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-02-2020, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T13:47:42-08:00","id":1427025,"title":"","content":"It depends what you mean. Like, the original Convention books aren't just told from a Tradition perspective; the Technocracy is really obviously bad news.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd say, Book of Chantries (so, book 3 I believe) at least presents some Technocrats as having good intentions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:13:12-08:00","id":1427030,"title":"","content":"They were always the good guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:16:46-08:00","id":1427034,"title":"","content":"I do recall Phil Brucato saying in an interview that he never liked the Technocracy as monolithically evil, and set out from the moment he got control of Mage (which was immediately after the core book was printed) to add more nuanced to them. So the Book of Chantries thing doesn't surprise me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T17:54:01-08:00","id":1427072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427030#post1427030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were always the good guys</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they're the materialist guys and the Traditions are the idealist guys. Both can be good or bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T20:37:44-08:00","id":1427093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427072#post1427072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say they're the materialist guys and the Traditions are the idealist guys. Both can be good or bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>One group being absolute jack holes to sleepers brought about the creation of the other soooo......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T21:05:47-08:00","id":1427096,"title":"","content":".....soooo the other became absolute jack holes to sleepers. <br /> <br /> Okay; that's an exaggeration. But then, so is the claim that the first group was absolute jack holes to Sleepers in the first place. <br /> <br /> It is true, though, that the Order of Reason lost its way; and by the time it reformed as the Technocracy, much of its original idealism was gone. And what followed was a gradual descent into arrogant control freakery. <i>Well intentioned</i> control freakery, for the most part; but you know what they say about the path to Hell and good intentions. By the time the Virtual Adepts abandoned them, everyone on both sides of the conflict had blood on their hands, and nobody had a clear claim to the moral high ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-07-2020, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T21:31:13-08:00","id":1427098,"title":"","content":"The Order of Reason started with that Proclamation of total eradication of [non-Christian?] wizards and genocide of all magical creatures. That isn't idealism, it's fanatical hatred. If they'd focused only on stomping out the Houses of Hermes (who really were absolute jack holes), and live and let live with other people, it would have been different.<br /> <br /> I can never see any group that has near-omnicidal genocide as their official policy as anything but absolutely evil. Individuals who joined the group have free will (more or less) and can be decent people, but not the Order itself. When you add authoritarianism, colonialism, racism, forced assimilation, exploitative capitalism, and mass mind control... well none of that is remotely close to good.<br /> <br /> I don't claim to know what official policies the Traditions have, in comparison. Other than the lack of omnicidal warfare against everyone else on Earth. It's the World of Darkness, so I suspect there are no genuine &quot;good guy&quot; groups, just shades of grey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  spelling typo 12-03-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T21:42:24-08:00","id":1427099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427093#post1427093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One group being absolute jack holes to sleepers brought about the creation of the other soooo......</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a compelling argument as to what the Technocracy and Traditions are portrayed as in modern books. Previous two replies covered the rest of anything I could possibly bring up.<br /> <br /> Materialism and idealism are philosophical concepts, though. Couldn't hurt to look them up.<br /> <br /> Google's first result is very simplified but not exactly wrong:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Idealism</b> is a branch of philosophy which says that idea precedes matter. It means, existence of matter is because of an idea of its existence. <b>Materialism</b> says matter precedes the idea. It means, an idea of the existence of a material is a result of its physical existence first. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T21:47:40-08:00","id":1427100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427098#post1427098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order of Reason started with that Proclamation of total eradication of [non-Christian?] wizards and genocide of all magical creatures. That isn't idealism, it's fanatical hatred.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's also an exaggeration. Sorcerers Crusade takes place roughly a century after the founding of the Order of Reason, and it shows us what the Order was like at that time. While they were antagonistic toward the fledgeling Traditions, it wasn't fanatical hatred, nor was it attempted genocide. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427098#post1427098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they'd focused only on stomping out the Houses of Hermes (who really were absolute jack holes)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they weren't; not overall. Sure, there were bad elements among them, such as the ones that the Craftsmasons took down early on; and that was enough to give them a bad rep. And no, they weren't pillars of virtue, either. But they weren't absolute jack holes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427098#post1427098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the World of Darkness, so I suspect there are no genuine &quot;good guy&quot; groups, just shades of grey.</div> </div> </div> </div> This, I absolutely agree with. Well, with the exception of the Nephandi. <i>They</i> are absolute jack holes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T21:53:19-08:00","id":1427101,"title":"","content":"I think it'd help to see a citation as to how every single Tradition were complete &quot;jack holes&quot; to sleepers. I'm definitely curious to see how such a disparate collection of magical practices are rooted in making life terrible for the general population, and how this claim isn't actually an overgeneralization.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious about how the kind of world that the Technocrats have built, with global warming, wealth inequality, massive amounts of waste, the developing world still being exploited to feed the developed world, means they are necessarily <i>good.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-03-2020, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T22:12:46-08:00","id":1427102,"title":"","content":"I will say this much: for all the bad things that have come with the Technocracy (and there are a lot of them), I still vastly prefer that over the world as it was when they were founded. And a significant amount of credit for the improvements goes to them. I won't go so far as to call them the <i>good guys</i>, because they're also responsible for so much bad stuff; but they're definitely not <i>all</i> bad. <br /> <br /> Shades of gray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T22:51:29-08:00","id":1427107,"title":"","content":"Are we sure they're telling the truth about the way the world was when magical tradition held sway, though? They have an entire wing dedicated to propaganda.<br /> <br /> My point wasn't that they're evil, though, but rather that calling them the good guys ignores or even actively sweeps a lot of excesses under the rug.<br /> <br /> Although a lot of stuff going on today wouldn't make the Technocracy look like humanity's saviors. Just... only those fortunate enough to live in the right place, or have the right parentage, or have the right opportunities. It's hard to argue a justification that the Technocracy's vision is all that great when one knows - for example - that enslaved children are forced to mine cobalt under hazardous conditions so we can have so many of those precious technological gadgets we rely upon so heavily.Making the Technocracy the face of institutions that have for centuries indulged in imperialist expansion and colonialist exploitation doesn't exactly put them in a good light.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T06:17:22-08:00","id":1427133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427101#post1427101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'd help to see a citation as to how every single Tradition were complete &quot;jack holes&quot; to sleepers. I'm definitely curious to see how such a disparate collection of magical practices are rooted in making life terrible for the general population, and how this claim isn't actually an overgeneralization.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious about how the kind of world that the Technocrats have built, with global warming, wealth inequality, massive amounts of waste, the developing world still being exploited to feed the developed world, means they are necessarily <i>good.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly don't know how the claim is so prevalent. I think it is some kind of strange assumption about the power and influence of the pre-Technocracy magical groups. Whatever the case it's great inspiration for Technocracy propaganda, but not so great for depicting early Traditions motivations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T06:31:10-08:00","id":1427134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427107#post1427107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we sure they're telling the truth about the way the world was when magical tradition held sway, though? They have an entire wing dedicated to propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Dark Ages: Mage (and, to a lesser extent, Cruzade) present those times as playable. We're as sure of how were the times before Technocratic predominance as it's possible to be sure of <i>anything at all</i><br /> <br /> Perhaps if we go further into the past, we could find times were history diverges...but, yeah, the world was pretty much as the popular depictions of our RL middle ages. Except that there were more monsters and magical beasts arround.<br /> <br /> One has to keep in mind that the Technocracy was founded against the Order of <s>Assholes</s> Hermes and the Messianic Voices. If those guys are your best reference of what's a mage, no wonder many hated mages (stupid mages, they ruined magick)<br /> <br /> <b>This clarification it's important however: </b>Starting point aside, we don't know how the world would look like if another magical faction had won predominance. We don't have any reason to think it would have turned out better.<br /> <br /> BUT, to say Technocracy with all it's evils were <i>necessary </i>to get out of the Middle Ages and bring our mostly better Modern Era comes dangerously close to the justifications used for<i> real life colonization</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>[irony]</b>Europe had to do what they had to do in order to <b><i>bring culture </i></b>to the world. They just couldn't leave<i> those poor savages</i> of the Native Americans <i>living like that</i> , w/o trains and stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - I'm sure things would be much worse for them if their cultures hadn't been burned to the ground, their land taken, their people enslaved... <b>[/irony]</b><br /> <br /> So, yeah, shades of gray. Also plenty of pitch black, mind you. Not all it's good intentions gone wrong.<br /> <br /> Their &quot;public&quot; agenda has many good selling points, but ultimately all the evil they did it's <i>*very* </i>hard to justify. To the point I would suspect the attempts of doing so as (very successful) fear-mongering propaganda from those above, spread because they want to remain in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-03-2020, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T06:38:10-08:00","id":1427135,"title":"","content":"No clue exactly when, but why is writing the Technocracy as a nuanced antagonist a bad thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T07:07:14-08:00","id":1427137,"title":"","content":"Who claimed the Technocracy gaining some nuance as a bad thing? If anything I feel like the Technocracy has been continuously been hammered ungracefully to be Totally Not The Bad Guys @TM to a point where I feel like continued attention keeps going on it instead of further developing the Traditions or breathing some life to the Disparates faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T07:15:37-08:00","id":1427138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427135#post1427135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No clue exactly when, but why is writing the Technocracy as a nuanced antagonist a bad thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing it's a nuanced antagonist. Another thing it's a &quot;Technocracy had to do what it had to do to avoid us living in the Dark Ages&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy it's nuanced because it started as a completely understandable rebelion against the magical overlords of Europe, and ended becoming corrupted.<br /> <br /> It started with idealists that had a &quot;power to the people&quot; agenda. But even from it's inception you have people like Wolfgang von Reisman, a power hungry money wizard that went in because he saw the opportunity to get power for himself, paying lip service to the agenda - and he wasn't a nobody, he founded the High Guild.<br /> <br /> These aren't just &quot;a loud minority&quot; - they're the <i>real </i>antagonists in a Technocracy game. Think that figthing against the Traditions when they're at their worst, with all the power of the Technocracy in your hands, would be like playing Mage in &quot;easy mode&quot;. It becomes hard when you have to fight the disconnection and/or corruption of your bosses at the same time.<br /> <br /> It has a lot of well intended people, and an agenda that's good on paper. But they're also a cold-blooded, murderous and power-hungry organization. Hence why you can see them as nuanced <i>antagonists</i> (to be defeated), and not <i>the actual good guys</i> (that you should join forces with) from the pov of the Traditions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-03-2020, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T07:34:32-08:00","id":1427139,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , agreed. What I don't get is why whenever these debates come up, every comment talking about a good or bad point about the Technocracy always seems to get interpreted as \u201cyou're saying that the Technocrats are the heroes/are the villains\u201d, when the truth is that they're a bit of both. <br /> <br /> To be clear, when I spoke of certain things being necessary, I was referring to instruments. In particular, I draw a distinction between Science and Technology on the one hand, and what you do with them on the other. Practice and Instruments are very much on the Science and Technology side of the equation where the technocracy is concerned (they're tools, with no inherent morality), and I was talking about how there is a certain advantage to Science and Technology in that regard. I was not talking about what the Technocracy or its predecessors in the Order of Reason did with technology. I agree that they have always had a self-righteousness to them, a sense that they know what's good for people better than the people know themselves. And whether that manifests as the Order of Reason seeking to \u201ccivilize savages\u201d against their will or the more modern Technocracy deciding that the Masses are too stupid to take care of themselves and need to be brought to heel, it's still the common thread of \u201cwe're the smart people, do as we say\u201d. <br /> <br /> The thing is, that's not unique to them. That's hubris, and it's a fault that <i>every</i> mage is prone to. And the more organized mages get, the more prone they are to that hubris. It tends to stand out more with the Technocracy largely because that's the most organized faction in the Ascension War; but it's present in all the factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-03-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T08:50:48-08:00","id":1427144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427100#post1427100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also an exaggeration. Sorcerers Crusade takes place roughly a century after the founding of the Order of Reason, and it shows us what the Order was like at that time. While they were antagonistic toward the fledgeling Traditions, it wasn't fanatical hatred, nor was it attempted genocide.<br /> <br /> Actually, they weren't; not overall. Sure, there were bad elements among them, such as the ones that the Craftsmasons took down early on; and that was enough to give them a bad rep. And no, they weren't pillars of virtue, either. But they weren't absolute jack holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, I didn't know that. I don't have Mage books, only the wiki to refer to. So, what <i>were</i> they like 100 years before the Proclamation of Fanatical Omnicide?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427102#post1427102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say this much: for all the bad things that have come with the Technocracy (and there are a lot of them), I still vastly prefer that over the world as it was when they were founded. And a significant amount of credit for the improvements goes to them. I won't go so far as to call them the <i>good guys</i>, because they're also responsible for so much bad stuff; but they're definitely not <i>all</i> bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only a nicer world if you're in the racially and economically privileged <i>minority</i>. It's <b>unambiguously much worse</b> if you're Native American, Australian Aboriginal, Bushman, or any number of other people whose entire social structure has been colonized/enslaved/smallpoxed out of existence, who are the oppressed, uninsured, disease-ridden, extremely impoverished, landless, disenfranchised, traumatized, police-brutalized, food-insecure, socially collapsed descendants of a tiny number of genocide survivors; or if you live in an island or country that's scheduled to sink into the ocean this century, or if you're a slave laborer. In the WoD it's also <i>unambiguously</i> worse for bygone beasts, shapeshifters, animal and plant spirits, fae, chimera, kinfolk, dreamers, the spirits of pre-Christian religions, the ghosts of all those genocided people, etc. Plus several ethnic groups that no longer exist at all due to successful genocide, countless species slaughtered to extinction, animals being tortured in factory farms, the two World Wars and Vietnam War and some Middle-Eastern wars that grew out of colonialism, the Great Maelstroms caused by colonization and World Wars, the entire biosphere of the whole planet on the verge of a profound collapse that will either wipe out humanity or create an even more desperate dystopia...<br /> <br /> Is this ecological collapse coming in M:tAs as well? If so, it's coming despite the Technocratic attempts to persuade the consensus that exploitative capitalism/neoimperialism isn't ruining the world, probably because the majority of human populations are on the receiving end of the factory and coal pollution, oil spills, fishery collapses, hills of garbage, exploitative near-slave labor, actual literal slave labor, growing inequality, plagues caused by environmental devastation, forced relocation, and local economic collapse, and <i>they know the propaganda is BS</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427134#post1427134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Europe had to do what they had to do in order to <b><i>bring culture </i></b>to the world. They just couldn't leave<i> those poor savages</i> of the Native Americans <i>living like that</i> , w/o trains and stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - I'm sure things would be much worse for them if their cultures hadn't been burned to the ground, their land taken, their people enslaved...</div> </div> </div> </div>100% this, and not ironic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427139#post1427139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get is why whenever these debates come up, every comment talking about a good or bad point about the Technocracy always seems to get interpreted as \u201cyou're saying that the Technocrats are the heroes/are the villains\u201d, when the truth is that they're a bit of both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was responding to this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427030#post1427030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were always the good guys</div> </div> </div> </div>Science and technology in the real world, and in the WoD, aren't exactly the same. For one thing, in the real world they haven't been hijacked by the Technocracy, so there's not this huge complex of censorship and fabricated data and propaganda manipulating the consensus and mutilating the scientific method. Not that I've seen, at least. For another thing, before the Technocrat victory, <i>magical healing actually worked</i>. It was possible to get your diseases treated by faith healers, magical herbalists, etc. IRL, these healers were numerous enough for most people to access them. So it just isn't true that science was the only possible cure for XYZ problems.<br /> <br /> To me the only ambiguity in the Technocracy is the free will their agents retain, in spite of Control. (I assume they have some free will or how could they be PCs?) As individuals, Technocrats can have very good intentions, within the constraints of their blinders and whatever group of people they favor, just like other playable characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  still trying to fix quote tag errors. 12-03-2020, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T09:23:13-08:00","id":1427148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427134#post1427134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Dark Ages: Mage (and, to a lesser extent, Cruzade) present those times as playable. We're as sure of how were the times before Technocratic predominance as it's possible to be sure of <i>anything at all</i><br /> <br /> Perhaps if we go further into the past, we could find times were history diverges...but, yeah, the world was pretty much as the popular depictions of our RL middle ages. Except that there were more monsters and magical beasts arround.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction: <b>Europe</b> was as depicted. That doesn't depict the people later colonized by Europeans. Croatan Song, for example, depicts the WoD's pre-Columbian North America as having a lot of times and places when life was pretty good for humans. Obviously there were also a few human-sacrifice cults, but today we continue to sacrifice human lives in &quot;sacrifice zones&quot; for corporate profit and middle-upper class white comfort, so what does that make us? Literal monsters have been replaced by police brutality and other white supremacist violence (and in the WoD the vampires are still around). I've spent last month reading about RL southern Africa, and life was pretty much paradise for the Bushmen and Khoekhoe before the Europeans, Herero, and Xhosa conquered them.<br /> <br /> Edit: I know none of the above is Mage canon, so YMMV/Your game may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-03-2020, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T09:44:42-08:00","id":1427153,"title":"","content":"Basically the Technocracy in my opinion (key word opinion), is just a catspaw for the Weaver. They just want the entire universe static of pure conformity and that's it. The M20 book, Chapter 5, part III directly tells you they want to eliminate all alternatives no matter what. Beside maybe trying to curtail whatever the Hermetics were doing, the rest of the Traditions before the formation of either faction don't give any tells they were Lord-Mages That Controlled and Oppressed Humanity @TM. They are just on a vindictive spree to monopolize their own repressed Paradigm across the world and control humanity. That seems pretty bad to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: (as a matter of fact we directly know some members of the &quot;Order of Reason&quot; / Technocracy were literally European Monarchs. Queen Victoria and Isabelle of Spain... from the lore blurbs of M20 in the history portion of the book... the Order of Reason doesn't have a favorable position of morality when the book literally is saying &quot;it initiated the three bloodiest atrocities in human history&quot; apparently.)<br /> <br /> Also even looking back the book directly, it affirms my previous claim that WAY to much focus is put on Technocracy than the other factions. Just literally look at how much pages the Technocracy part of the book compared to the Traditions before it or the Disparates after it? LOL. Not only that its also getting more books for M20 still.. have any other books even propped up for the others yet?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For another thing, before the Technocrat victory, <i>magical healing actually worked</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Magickal healing still works. It can be done safely if done Coincidentally or if need to be done in an extreme case, done Vulgarly; which only generates one point of Paradox as long as you don't Botch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-03-2020, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T09:55:20-08:00","id":1427157,"title":"","content":"You're right but to be fair, they are Weaver tools only within crossover. In Mage alone the relevant force is Stasis. I don't know to what extent the Technocrats are 'pawns' of Stasis (as opposed to just pawns of Control), whether Stasis is alive or sentient, or how else it differs from Werewolf's Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T09:57:50-08:00","id":1427158,"title":"","content":"And there's that \u201cthey're pitch black evil\u201d thing again. Every time anyone mentions something good that they did, you immediately counter with \u201cbut they also did this really horrible thing too\u201d. The implication being that the really horrible thing completely and utterly renders the good thing irrelevant. <br /> <br /> Remember, I'm not the one who said that they're the good guys; I was one of the first to <i>challenge</i> the guy who said that they're the good guys. I'm the one saying that it's a shades of gray thing. And you don't have to concentrate solely on the bad to show that they're not all or even mostly good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:03:12-08:00","id":1427160,"title":"","content":"The 1e concept of the Technocracy, Marauders, and Nephandi was that they were agents of the Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm, respectively. Mage has come a long way since then, and the current stance (spelled out in M20) is that this is an overly simplified view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:14:27-08:00","id":1427162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427158#post1427158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's that \u201cthey're pitch black evil\u201d thing again. Every time anyone mentions something good that they did, you immediately counter with \u201cbut they also did this really horrible thing too\u201d. The implication being that the really horrible thing completely and utterly renders the good thing irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually. I'm pointing out that making a small minority of people rich at the expense of hundreds of millions (or billions?) of atrocity victims <i>is not a good thing at all.</i> Colonial exploitation is <b>fundamentally a bad thing</b>, full stop, even if you and I benefit personally. The so-called good things you keep praising are not &quot;also&quot; or separate from the acts of atrocity, they are the <i>spoils of war</i>.<br /> <br /> I've also repeatedly acknowledged that as individuals, Technocrats can do good deeds like that NWO agent who was trying to stop the drug thing. Please do not exaggerate or misrepresent what I'm writing.<br /> <br /> I am clearly, obviously, distinguishing the structure of the organization from the agency of individuals embedded within it. That important distinction is a fact both of the Technocracy, and of us beneficiaries of colonialism IRL, so don't start accusing me of personal attacks next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-03-2020, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:41:40-08:00","id":1427168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427148#post1427148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correction: <b>Europe</b> was as depicted. That doesn't depict the people later colonized by Europeans. Croatan Song, for example, depicts the WoD's pre-Columbian North America as having a lot of times and places when life was pretty good for humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Maybe other places were more idylic in the mystic past, but wasn't the case everywhere. In China the Wu Lung (a craft of aristocratic mages) had a firm grip on the Consensus, and probably not the best interests of the minorities in mind. Don't know elsewhere<br /> <br /> But the Order of Reason started in Europe with the Craftmasons, and, as I said, their experiences with mages and the supernatural were the Order of Hermes, mage-hating Garou, the Tremere. More so, Mage factions in Europe were at war before the OoR was founded. The christian Messianic Voices were hunting witches and monsters before it was cool.<br /> <br /> Now, in all these conflicts the ones that suffer the most are those without powers. And Crafmasons venerated hard work, and thus they had commoners in a very high pedestal. So the fact all of these supernaturals predated on the commoners was a big no for them. At first they tried to transform the Order of Hermes from the inside, but after the Order ignored the diabolical predation uppon mortals from the Hermetic Chantry called Mistridge (because the victims were just mortals), they decided to take the matter in their own hands, and armed the people with magical weapons to kill the mages<br /> <br /> After that was the only thing that worked, it's only natural they would think hostile supernaturals answer only to iron...and this mentality was carried to the Order of reason they would found.<br /> <br /> So, in part, that's why they decided hunt the supernatural. Still, I think that the main reason of why the Order of Reason jumped into the imperialistic boats of the colonization era it's rather mundane: power corrupts<br /> <br /> At the begining the Order was much more tame. It included mystical practices as members, and were much more willing to listen. They focused on killing the mosters they deemed dangerous - they didn't know Paradox existed, much less that could be weaponized to destroy all the supernatural, only in Cruzade it starts being discovered (and in that era, it was against the old Technocracy more than against mystics)<br /> <br /> After they managed to won in Europe, however, they got <i>loads </i>of power. And you know that power corrupts: They wanted to rule <i>over</i> humanity in a perfect world created by them (mages will be mages?) . That's the corruption of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It's Hubris more than malice, really, because most believe they will, eventually, make a better world for everyone - something that the ignorant masses can't be trusted to do on their own (and, in fact, will point at the many tragedies brought by technology as &quot;the masses&quot; abusing the power they were given - which it's insulting, because they <i>never</i> recognize any <i>positive </i>scientific feat to &quot;the masses&quot;. But I disgress).<br /> <br /> But it's also malice. A desire of absolut power and control. It's a very humane, and very mage, motivation. They're far from the only mage organization that did terrible things in the name of the &quot;greater good&quot;, with a hidden (or not so hidden) desire for power...but on them it <i>shows </i>because they have a lot more power than most mages to <i>enact </i>this Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-03-2020, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T11:09:19-08:00","id":1427173,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Your focusing entirely on how the technocracy went about it, and completely dismissing the good things that came out of it. Electricity, optics, and so on and so forth. I'm not saying that colonialism is good, or that electricity<br /> <br /> I agree that the history behind it is sordid. I have never said otherwise. but you seem to be saying that they're accomplishments don't mean anything because of how they did it. And what's particularly bad about that is that they didn't have to do it that way. Electricity, optics, and so on and so forth could have been achieved without the colonialism.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that colonialism is good, or that electricity makes colonialism acceptable. I'm saying that colonialism is bad, but that that doesn't make electricity bad. The Technocracy did a good thing in introducing electricity, seven though they did it in a very horrifying way. <br /> <br /> The fact that we have electricity is a good thing. The fact that people have suffered in the process is a bad thing. The latter does <i>not</i> automatically render the former moot, any more than the former renders the latter moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T11:21:15-08:00","id":1427174,"title":"","content":"Its funny however.. because couldn't a Mystic based Awakened with Forces introduce electricity just as easily without the Technocracy eventually? No need for &quot;Pograms&quot; (yes, this is a term the Technocracy uses), hoarding wealth and repressing the Masses (High Guild/Syndicate), or destroying every other viewpoint until everything is one static reality (Technocracy's MO). However this isn't to say the Technocracy can't do any good in some facets or margin.. but yeah...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T11:34:43-08:00","id":1427176,"title":"","content":"Absolutely, it could have been done without all of the colonialist and related stuff. And you wouldn't even have needed to go with a different group to accomplish that. If you read The sorcerer's crusade material, you'll note that the Craftmasons are depicted as the conscience of the Order of Reason; they're the ones who are looking at some of the goals of the other Conventions and saying, \u201cthat might not be such a good idea\u201d, while organizing themselves in a way to counter the worst impulses of their fellow Conventions. From what I've heard, the authorial intent was that the purge of the Craftmasons was the point that the Order of Reason lost its way. <br /> <br /> In an alternate history where the Craftmasons were more successful in tempering the worst impulses of their fellow Conventions, you could easily have a modern day Order of Reason that introduced all of the good things that the Technocracy did in a more humane way. <br /> <br /> but again, the fact that electricity could have been introduced in a more humane way does not mean that it is bad that electricity was introduced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T11:51:29-08:00","id":1427178,"title":"","content":"I think that one of the factors in the Technocracy becoming more controlling and aloof from the Masses is the very real goal of developing Enlightened Science further. Why spend time improving the world while there are new Procedures of 4 and 5 levels (and possibly beyond) to be created? Back in the days of the Order of Reason there seems to have been an attitude that through planning, cunning, and brave hearts the Fellowship members will prevail. While with the shift towards Technocracy, and the final establishment of it, a desire and pursuit of excellence in Hypertechnology were put forward as a priority. So the Syndicate is very interested in just how much and in what ways they can tweak the Masses and whole economies; the New World Order has a priority on barely comprehensible psychological experiments etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T12:04:02-08:00","id":1427180,"title":"","content":"Just because one portion of the Order of Reason was more liberal or humane than the other factions never meant it was good since its inception, its naive to say they &quot;lost their way&quot; just from the Craftmasons being removed. And no one is saying or disputes the invention of electricity is bad at all; its just that literally any other Awakened/Enlightened person could've &quot;discovered&quot; it at any point of time without the Technocracy like I post earlier. The Technocrats also claim they were the ones &quot;upseating the &quot;&quot;Mages&quot;&quot; who lorded over humanity&quot; when conversely we know practically the entire history of the Order of Reason and then Technocracy has operated in the highest echelons of mortal government, or sometimes the Head of State of such polities as we see with Queen Victoria and Queen Isabella (who was part of the Cabal of Pure Thought btw.. the one Convention associated with burning people to death or any finding any &quot;Heretics&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-03-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T12:08:33-08:00","id":1427182,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a>, that's more or less what I was getting at with my comments about the Craftmasons: while they were in the Order of Reason, they were always insisting that there be an ethic to whatever the Order did: not Science for its own sake, but Science to empower the common man. After they were removed, the Order and then Technocracy continued to pay lip service to that ideal, but wandered further and further away from it in practice \u2014 so that now, they're viewing the Masses as a danger that must be subjugated for their own good. <br /> <br /> In my games, I've gone with the Navalon plot; and I'm treating Navalon as the spiritual heirs of the Craftmasons. Enlightened Science all the way; but with an ethic guiding it, and that ethic being the empowerment of the Sleepers to live their own lives and make their own choices. Which makes them the anti-Technocracy, in that they stand opposed to the notion that the Enlightened should be controlling the Masses. Technocrats may have the smarts; but they lack the wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T12:32:18-08:00","id":1427184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427168#post1427168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Order of Reason started in Europe with the Craftmasons, and, as I said, their experiences with mages and the supernatural were the Order of Hermes, mage-hating Garou, the Tremere. More so, Mage factions in Europe were at war before the OoR was founded. The christian Messianic Voices were hunting witches and monsters before it was cool.<br /> <br /> Now, in all these conflicts the ones that suffer the most are those without powers. And Crafmasons venerated hard work, and thus they had commoners in a very high pedestal. So the fact all of these supernaturals predated on the commoners was a big no for them. At first they tried to transform the Order of Hermes from the inside, but after the Order ignored the diabolical predation uppon mortals from the Hermetic Chantry called Mistridge (because the victims were just mortals), they decided to take the matter in their own hands, and armed the people with magical weapons to kill the mages<br /> <br /> After that was the only thing that worked, it's only natural they would think hostile supernaturals answer only to iron...and this mentality was carried to the Order of reason they would found.<br /> <br /> So, in part, that's why they decided hunt the supernatural. Still, I think that the main reason of why the Order of Reason jumped into the imperialistic boats of the colonization era it's rather mundane: power corrupts<br /> <br /> At the begining the Order was much more tame. It included mystical practices as members, and were much more willing to listen. They focused on killing the mosters they deemed dangerous - they didn't know Paradox existed, much less that could be weaponized to destroy all the supernatural, only in Cruzade it starts being discovered (and in that era, it was against the old Technocracy more than against mystics)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the very interesting stuff to me, because it's not a story I can find easily online. What the Order was doing before the Declaration of the (White Tower?). The idea of common mortals having best interests -- although there was an inevitable power-corruption in this: in the WoD, like in Exalted, the common mortals <i>can't</i> champion themselves democratically because only people with magic powers can change the world in major ways, so any such protection is inherently unrepresentative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427173#post1427173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the history behind it is sordid. I have never said otherwise. but you seem to be saying that they're accomplishments don't mean anything because of how they did it. And what's particularly bad about that is that they didn't have to do it that way. Electricity, optics, and so on and so forth could have been achieved without the colonialism.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that colonialism is good, or that electricity makes colonialism acceptable. I'm saying that colonialism is bad, but that that doesn't make electricity bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you for specifying! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The <i>wealth</i> that white and Han people have stolen is bad no matter who benefits, and I thought you were talking about <i>that</i>. But there is a list of things that (in the WoD) have been championed by the Technocracy that <b>didn't</b> and still don't require colonialization or fossil fuels:<ul><li>Electricity, if gained via solar panels (fun fact: IRL solar energy was invented at the same time as the internal combustion engine. We could have been using solar energy <i>all this time</i>.)</li> <li>Water sanitization</li> <li>Telecommunications (in Werewolf this is a Weaver web thing, but I can imagine it's less ambiguous in Mage)</li> <li>Internet access (started out democratic with free speech, now that's being taken away)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Or the list of things the Technocrats champion that aren't related to fossil fuels and mass murder at all, like:<ul><li>Fighting the Dark Masters of Zeernogibberish out in the Dark Umbra, so they don't invade Earth.</li> <li>Opposing the f***ed-up anti-vaxxer movement, which I'd guess also exists in the WoD.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Let's talk about these <i>unambiguously good things</i> instead!<br /> <br /> They could potentially try to convince people that rhino horns, pangolin scales, and tiger balls don't have magic powers, although I don't know if they actually do work on that. Or if it really is about magic anymore, but rather the status symbol.<br /> <br /> They could have invented personal computers and cell phones that didn't rely on cobalt or rare earth minerals or plastic, too... but they didn't, and now the consensus has cemented these requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  typos, paragraph breaks 12-03-2020, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T12:43:33-08:00","id":1427187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427180#post1427180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because one portion of the Order of Reason was more liberal or humane than the other factions never meant was good since its inception, its naive to say they &quot;lost their way&quot; just from the Craftmasons being removed..</div> </div> </div> </div>They were't just &quot;one portion&quot;, though. They were it's founders and the ones who crafted the initial agenda.<br /> <br /> That being said, yeah, of course that they didn't &quot;went bad&quot; from one day to the other. Since it's inception there were nasty elements crawling into it...but that happens to the best organizations.<br /> <br /> The slow declive, and final extermination, of the Craftmasons at the hands of their own creation mark the moments where the elements in the Order that wanted power over the world gained predominance. Finally, in the Victorian Era, they abandoned any pretense and started calling themselves &quot;Technocracy&quot;, symbolically leaving the ideals of Reason aside<br /> <br /> But the original idea of figthing against the darkness wasn't wrong given the situation of Europe at the time. The idea of empowering the masses by giving them the tools wasn't wrong (and, ultimately, was the reason why the Craftmasons were purged - the rest of the Technocracy felt they were giving too much, and wanted to protect their magely privileges. So the masons had to go).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no one is saying or disputes the invention of electricity is bad at all; its just that literally any other Awakened/Enlightened person could've &quot;discovered&quot; it at any point of time without the Technocracy like I post earlier. </div> </div> </div>Well, that we don't know. Because they didn't. All that we know it's that the Technocrats were able to pull it off - we don't know how much your Paradigm has to be encroached in the Consensus in order to do that, or what are the exact steps to make something magical into something mundane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocrats also claim they were the ones &quot;upseating the &quot;&quot;Mages&quot;&quot; who lorded over humanity&quot; when conversely we know practically the entire history of the Order of Reason and then Technocracy has operated in the highest echelons of mortal government, or sometimes the Head of State of such polities as we see with Queen Victoria and Queen Isabella (who was part of the Cabal of Pure Thought btw.. the one Convention associated with burning people to death or any finding any &quot;Heretics&quot;) </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy have been on top for a while, but that doesn't mean that in their inception they weren't the underdogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T12:59:19-08:00","id":1427190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427182#post1427182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a>, that's more or less what I was getting at with my comments about the Craftmasons: while they were in the Order of Reason, they were always insisting that there be an ethic to whatever the Order did: not Science for its own sake, but Science to empower the common man. After they were removed, the Order and then Technocracy continued to pay lip service to that ideal, but wandered further and further away from it in practice \u2014 so that now, they're viewing the Masses as a danger that must be subjugated for their own good.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I'd add there is that I believe there's an element of writing.. maybe not failure but something like that.<br /> <br /> We know much of the Technocracy was written with deliberate irony. The writers have said as much repeatedly. You're supposed to notice the dissonance between the way the books are written and the things the characters actually do. Like, the characters are nice and they talk a good game, but they're actually part of this pretty awful organisation.<br /> <br /> However, I found that that failed with the Craftmasons. You're clearly right that that's what the authors intended, was for the Craftmasons to be the well-meaning group that get the bump, however, reading Sorcerer's Crusade, I personally find them among the most suspect of the conventions. Their dream of a world run by them without the common people knowing is... Not great, and combined with the pseudo-masonic iconography... well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T13:22:25-08:00","id":1427196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427184#post1427184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the very interesting stuff to me, because it's not a story I can find easily online. What the Order was doing before the Declaration of the (White Tower?). The idea of common mortals having best interests -- although there was an inevitable power-corruption in this: in the WoD, like in Exalted, the common mortals <i>can't</i> champion themselves democratically because only people with magic powers can change the world in major ways, so any such protection is inherently unrepresentative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ultimately true; but it's possible for the Awakened to mitigate this. The more Sleepers can do on their own, the less the Awakened have to do for them; and the more democratic and in charge of their own fate the Sleepers can be. <br /> <br /> Of course, the Technocracy counters that argument by pointing to just how stupid the Sleepers have been with the gifts already afforded them. They do not trust the Sleepers (with good reason, they argue), and because of this they seek to subvert democratic systems so that they can overrule the Sleepers whenever they think they're being stupid. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427184#post1427184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thank you for specifying! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The <i>wealth</i> that white and Han people have stolen is bad no matter who benefits, and I thought you were talking about <i>that</i>. But there is a list of things that (in the WoD) have been championed by the Technocracy that <b>didn't</b> and still don't require colonialization or fossil fuels:<ul><li>Electricity, if gained via solar panels (fun fact: IRL solar energy was invented at the same time as the internal combustion engine. We could have been using solar energy <i>all this time</i>.)</li> <li>Water sanitization</li> <li>Telecommunications (in Werewolf this is a Weaver web thing, but I can imagine it's less ambiguous in Mage)</li> <li>Internet access (started out democratic with free speech, now that's being taken away)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Or the list of things the Technocrats champion that aren't related to fossil fuels and mass murder at all, like:<ul><li>Fighting the Dark Masters of Zeernogibberish out in the Dark Umbra, so they don't invade Earth.</li> <li>Opposing the f***ed-up anti-vaxxer movement, which I'd guess also exists in the WoD.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Let's talk about these <i>unambiguously good things</i> instead!<br /> <br /> They could potentially try to convince people that rhino horns, pangolin scales, and tiger balls don't have magic powers, although I don't know if they actually do work on that. Or if it really is about magic anymore, but rather the status symbol.<br /> <br /> They could have invented personal computers and cell phones that didn't rely on cobalt or rare earth minerals or plastic, too... but they didn't, and now the consensus has cemented these requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they could have come up with a more humane way to acquire the special ingredients. (By the way: are you aware that solar panels require rare earth elements as well? Solar power looks like a good option until you look into just what is needed to make them.)<br /> <br /> One reason behind my Earthly foundations argument is to come up with a reason why an Enlightened Scientist might have chosen to go with arbitrary choices like requiring rare earth elements, why the Void Engineers formatting of space into Conventional Space results in a vacuum, and so on. In short, the decision to do things the way they did was more involved than just arbitrary, capricious, pointless choices. \u201cThis is what you have to do in order to maintain full compatibility with the Earthly Foundations\u201d becomes the reason why the Enlightened Scientists went with the technology that they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T13:59:06-08:00","id":1427198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they didn't. All that we know it's that the Technocrats were able to pull it off - we don't know how much your Paradigm has to be encroached in the Consensus in order to do that, or what are the exact steps to make something magical into something mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>You told me before the in the lore of Ascension in another thread, it was always Awakened folk or some matter who advanced technology no matter what right? If we take that and extrapolate, Awakenings keep happening regardless and technological progress would've kept advancing no matter what albeit maybe at a different pace or no change in pace at all. The fact that they only formed in the Middle-Ages shows that irregardless of them, technology still advanced, because if nothing else humanity would still be in Paleolithic times. Whether operating on an Arete or Enlightened Paradigm, tech still progresses because the supply of Awakened is always constant with humanity being constant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but that doesn't mean that in their inception they weren't the underdogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>When was the Order of Reason EVER the underdogs? When literally the majority of their history is invading other places and enforcing static Paradigm? The history blurb of M20 directly tells us they used Portugal and Spain to &quot;spread the Ascension&quot; war around the globe... to parties that weren't even privy to it whatsoever. It also doesn't help that they literally since its near beginning have had European monarchs in its direct control or like I said before; The Technocracy/Order of Reason have been at the &quot;top&quot; since the very beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's inception there were nasty elements crawling into it...but that happens to the best organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this mean? The nasty elements of the Order of Reason have been in the faction since it's beginning, &quot;not crawled into it&quot;. The Cabal of Pure Thought (Gabrialites), High-Guild, and Void-Seekers (Explorators), Celestial Masters... all contributed to the atrocities that the Order of Reason committed and their policy still influences the modern successor, the Technocracy.. Its very generous to even claim the Craftmasons were even in control of this organization from the beginning just because they founded it or if its proported ideals were the de-facto reality of it from the get-go.<br /> <br /> Honestly I just feel like the Order of Reason was founded by the Craftmasons just to get back at the Hermetic Order over disputes of how magick should be handled, but now its backfired on them badly (well, they're dead now..) and the Technocracy is the exact OPPOSITE of what they've wanted. And for their little feud against just the Hermetic Order, now the other mystics who had no involvement to it have been dragged in. The Traditions literally formed as a response to the Order of Reasons aggression against everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-07-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T14:25:28-08:00","id":1427201,"title":"","content":"I'm going to concur with <i>Book of Shadows</i> as the first significant work making the Technocracy less evil from an written for the players of the game perspective. The convention books are pro-Technocracy and some of them are pretty bad in the first edition in terms of their views--the Progenitors seem much more like complete jackasses in that book than in the later convention book.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Mage is a nuanced game and you can find all sorts of evidence for horrible mages in each faction if you're willing to dig hard enough. So, the debate here is mostly about the eternal problem of Mage: all these people had great power and great responsibility and ranking their failures is depends on what you consider a failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T14:26:29-08:00","id":1427202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427196#post1427196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is ultimately true; but it's possible for the Awakened to mitigate this. The more Sleepers can do on their own, the less the Awakened have to do for them; and the more democratic and in charge of their own fate the Sleepers can be.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Technocracy counters that argument by pointing to just how stupid the Sleepers have been with the gifts already afforded them. They do not trust the Sleepers (with good reason, they argue), and because of this they seek to subvert democratic systems so that they can overrule the Sleepers whenever they think they're being stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they're right about both... except that they're just as stupid and destructive and corrupted as the rest of humanity.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Garou make the same exact arguments for why they need to control humanity. Although in the non-consensual W:tA cosmology, their religion is objectively correct and the actions of humanity are even more destructive to the fundament of reality. But of course, they're corrupted and fallible and guilty of many atrocities, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427196#post1427196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(By the way: are you aware that solar panels require rare earth elements as well? Solar power looks like a good option until you look into just what is needed to make them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and some require lead. It's not perfectly clean, but also <b>not biosphere-destroying</b>. Although IRL there's hope it can become 100% clean. And speaking of alternatives, even burning wood causes tons of environmental destruction, greenhouse pollution, human health problems, and even landslides. But despite that Wood and solar are still <b>vastly</b> safer and more humane than coal or gas. There's no RL scenario in which solar is <i>not</i> a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427196#post1427196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason behind my Earthly foundations argument is to come up with a reason why an Enlightened Scientist might have chosen to go with arbitrary choices like requiring rare earth elements, why the Void Engineers formatting of space into Conventional Space results in a vacuum, and so on. In short, the decision to do things the way they did was more involved than just arbitrary, capricious, pointless choices. \u201cThis is what you have to do in order to maintain full compatibility with the Earthly Foundations\u201d becomes the reason why the Enlightened Scientists went with the technology that they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they were operating according to their own paradigm. They didn't realize that with Magick they could arbitrarily select anything at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-03-2020, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T17:33:26-08:00","id":1427224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427198#post1427198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You told me before the in the lore of Ascension in another thread, it was always Awakened folk or some matter who advanced technology no matter what right? If we take that and extrapolate, Awakenings keep happening regardless and technological progress would've kept advancing no matter what albeit maybe at a different pace or no change in pace at all. The fact that they only formed in the Middle-Ages shows that irregardless of them, technology still advanced, because if nothing else humanity would still be in Paleolithic times. Whether operating on an Arete or Enlightened Paradigm, tech still progresses because the supply of Awakened is always constant with humanity being constant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah,. However, that Awakened folk are supposed to be pivotal to the development of science and technology doesn't mean that all Awakened folk will advance technolgy.<br /> <br /> This happens, but there are gray areas.<br /> <br /> Human development isn't a constant, and while the advantages of modernity to the peoples of the world are debatable, nobody debates that there was a <i>tremendous </i>surge of science and technology after the age of enligthenment.<br /> <br /> In Mage, Technocracy it's the faction that represents that advance. The luxuries and power it brought to the west, and the sufferings it brought too. Now, while I don't think Technocrats are essential to human development, I think there's many open questions about how this development would be.<br /> <br /> Like, we know that the Consensus it's important for this because the Technocracy manipulates the Consensus to introduce new tech at their own pace. But we don't know, for instance, how many people has to believe in a certain type of magick before it becomes, not just Coincident, but commonplace. The more people you need to convince,the harder it will be to do so without stepping on someone's toes and causing a conflict.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> has the theory that Technomagick has a clear advantage at the time of solidifying Reality as to make effects commonplace. I'm not so certain about that... Still, it holds water. Most of the technology in WoD it's, well, <i>technological</i>. So it stands to reason that techomagic has an advantage (hence they won). Or not - maybe it's because the Traditions hadn't thought (or believed) in making their mojo something everyone can use (and the Technocracy just did it first). And these aren't the only posibilities. There's no definite answer here.<br /> <br /> If mages don't care about developping humans, the technological development migth slow to a crawl, stop or even recede (there were times in history where technology was lost). Depending on how much this slows advancement, it could take a lot of time to reach the point where electricity is a thing<br /> <br /> Also mages could develop humanity in a completely different way - more spiritual and less materialistic - where electricity isn't seen as a need.<br /> <br /> We <i>really </i>don't know how the world would look like without Technocrats. There's a lot of worlbuilding potential here. Hence it's a bit lazzy to say everyone could've done the same. True, that's not impossible, but it's not the obvious outcome either.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, my point was that what they did isn't insignificant. They, among all mages, have that &quot;achievement&quot;. For good or ill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When was the Order of Reason EVER the underdogs? </div> </div> </div>At the start of the Sorcerer's Cruzade they were the underdogs who had to hide and act with subtlety. At that time the Scourge (aka, Paradox) was very much against them, and the joined force of the Traditions should have crushed them - but, of course, the Traditions had way to many hatchets to burry back then, and couldn't keep a cohesive opposition (I know, that's the history of the Traditions - but it was much worse back then. Like, just reading what Master LaSalle had to do in order to *force* the OoH into the Traditions should be enough to note what a tense alliance it was)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does this mean? The nasty elements of the Order of Reason have been in the faction since it's beginning, &quot;not crawled into it&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. But they had to join at some point - even if that point was the Convocation itself.<br /> <br /> I would assume not all the people who joined the OoR were paying lip service to the idea of helping humanity. Even if each had their own idea of how to do so. Most probably weren't any more evil than your average Tradition mage.<br /> <br /> Void-Seekers and Celestial Masters are a good example. They weren't real factions before joining, they were largely random individuals that liked exploration magic, and were largely incapable of conquering anything. But thanks to the resources of the Guild and the armies of the Gabrielites, that changed. They were given power, and the task of spreading the Bible and the coin. And this was even before the age of colonization started.<br /> <br /> If Craftmasons were innocent at something, was at thinking *their* mystical order wasn't going to fall to Hubris and want the power for themselves...<br /> <br /> However they weren't saints either. They had solid reasons to do what they did in Europe, and lofty goals, but *were* willing to use extreme measures to reach them. Like allowing the Gabrielites to join. That was one risky move. However, facts are: If you want to fight &quot;the dark&quot;, you need an army capable of figthing monsters and wizards. The Gabrielites were already doing that, and thus they were allowed to join even when almost nobody in the Order liked them<br /> <br /> Notably, after the Gabrielites were betrayed by the Union some joined the nascent NWO, some went back to the Celestial Chorus, and the rest formed the Knigths Templar (now Disparate Alliance). To show the OoR aren't the only Mage faction to welcome extra firepower with open arms regardless of morality or past deeds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-03-2020, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T17:36:32-08:00","id":1427225,"title":"","content":"Loving <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar896_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"896\" data-vbnamecard=\"896\">Erinys</a> posts, btw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427133#post1427133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't know how the claim is so prevalent. I think it is some kind of strange assumption about the power and influence of the pre-Technocracy magical groups. Whatever the case it's great inspiration for Technocracy propaganda, but not so great for depicting early Traditions motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels kind of iconoclastic, like &quot;well you thought they were the heroes&quot; but over time stuff changes and even people<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427134#post1427134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Dark Ages: Mage (and, to a lesser extent, Cruzade) present those times as playable. We're as sure of how were the times before Technocratic predominance as it's possible to be sure of <i>anything at all</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages Mage takes place during a time when we already know Hermetic magic specifically was becoming less effective. The Tremere tried to do their immortality spell before the time that line covered because the longevity elixirs (or whatever they're called I don't have Ars Magica handy) were becoming less effective and starting to fail, so I don't think it's really fair or accurate to mark that place during that period of time as the magical traditions being dominant, and thus an example of how the traditions (or rather the groups that became the Traditions) treated people poorly.<br /> <br /> It's especially telling since the oldest known human settlement on Earth goes back at least 11,000 years - that being the city of Jericho in what is now the West Bank. So we have like maybe 9% of history to go on in the WoD in this particular case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427134#post1427134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps if we go further into the past, we could find times were history diverges...but, yeah, the world was pretty much as the popular depictions of our RL middle ages. Except that there were more monsters and magical beasts arround.<br /> <br /> One has to keep in mind that the Technocracy was founded against the Order of <s>Assholes</s> Hermes and the Messianic Voices. If those guys are your best reference of what's a mage, no wonder many hated mages (stupid mages, they ruined magick)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been ages since I read about the Order of Reason's assault on Doissetep or their reasons for doing so. I know the Technocratic line is that the Order of Hermes was abusing people and that's certainly not implausible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427134#post1427134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>This clarification it's important however: </b>Starting point aside, we don't know how the world would look like if another magical faction had won predominance. We don't have any reason to think it would have turned out better.<br /> <br /> BUT, to say Technocracy with all it's evils were <i>necessary </i>to get out of the Middle Ages and bring our mostly better Modern Era comes dangerously close to the justifications used for<i> real life colonization</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>[irony]</b>Europe had to do what they had to do in order to <b><i>bring culture </i></b>to the world. They just couldn't leave<i> those poor savages</i> of the Native Americans <i>living like that</i> , w/o trains and stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - I'm sure things would be much worse for them if their cultures hadn't been burned to the ground, their land taken, their people enslaved... <b>[/irony]</b><br /> <br /> So, yeah, shades of gray. Also plenty of pitch black, mind you. Not all it's good intentions gone wrong.<br /> <br /> Their &quot;public&quot; agenda has many good selling points, but ultimately all the evil they did it's <i>*very* </i>hard to justify. To the point I would suspect the attempts of doing so as (very successful) fear-mongering propaganda from those above, spread because they want to remain in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this clarification, btw. I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427153#post1427153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically the Technocracy in my opinion (key word opinion), is just a catspaw for the Weaver. They just want the entire universe static of pure conformity and that's it. The M20 book, Chapter 5, part III directly tells you they want to eliminate all alternatives no matter what. Beside maybe trying to curtail whatever the Hermetics were doing, the rest of the Traditions before the formation of either faction don't give any tells they were Lord-Mages That Controlled and Oppressed Humanity @TM. They are just on a vindictive spree to monopolize their own repressed Paradigm across the world and control humanity. That seems pretty bad to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Weaver no doubt loves what they're doing but honestly there's no reason to set up the Technocracy as the Weaver's Pentex. They can be free willed doing all this.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm going to say that the Technocratic Paradigm does not in fact put magic in the hands of the &quot;common man.&quot; It puts it in the hands of presidents, prime ministers, billionaires, corporations, etc. and everyone not fortunate enough to be wealthy and/or powerful gets what they want to allow them. Capitalism is very much the Syndicate's thing and it's also very much an elitist thing at this point in history, and was only a bit better for a few decades in a few places. Much of the rest of the world sees far less benefit and far more exploitation.<br /> <br /> That a single mother needs to work three full time jobs to support her kids is an abject failure of the stated goal to &quot;put magic in the hands of the common person.&quot; The Technocracy's problem is that they're presented as the curators of the modern world, not so much trying to change it as trying to ensure no one else can. This means, unless the WoD becomes decisively better than the real world thanks to Technocrat involvement, they're responsible for a lot of truly awful things. And any representation of them should be honest about that.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they're 100% evil. I'm saying the stuff happening on their watch isn't justifiable, and makes it nigh-impossible for them to collectively be the good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T18:40:26-08:00","id":1427239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427224#post1427224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or not - maybe it's because the Traditions hadn't thought (or believed) in making their mojo something everyone can use (and the Technocracy just did it first).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Order of Reason did it first, but surely some of the Cult of Ecstasy worked very hard to make it so anyone can cook meth in their basement!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427225#post1427225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm going to say that the Technocratic Paradigm does not in fact put magic in the hands of the &quot;common man.&quot; It puts it in the hands of presidents, prime ministers, billionaires, corporations, etc. and everyone not fortunate enough to be wealthy and/or powerful gets what they want to allow them. Capitalism is very much the Syndicate's thing and it's also very much an elitist thing at this point in history, and was only a bit better for a few decades in a few places. Much of the rest of the world sees far less benefit and far more exploitation.<br /> <br /> That a single mother needs to work three full time jobs to support her kids is an abject failure of the stated goal to &quot;put magic in the hands of the common person.&quot; The Technocracy's problem is that they're presented as the curators of the modern world, not so much trying to change it as trying to ensure no one else can. This means, unless the WoD becomes decisively better than the real world thanks to Technocrat involvement, they're responsible for a lot of truly awful things. And any representation of them should be honest about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right, but I don't think anyone's saying the average Technocrat gives a crap about commoners <i>anymore</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, capitalist was always completely elitist, with the &quot;common good&quot; as pure propaganda, but I can imagine that some Order of Reason ites (sp?) had honest populist intentions centuries before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  should make a new post instead of editing this one 12-03-2020, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T18:42:40-08:00","id":1427240,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I just wanted to restate my reasons for initially stating that they're not really the good guys. They're not unambiguously the bad guys either, there's lots of room for good and bad in the group.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T18:52:48-08:00","id":1427241,"title":"","content":"I think that as a splat design, it would be easier to depict Technocratic PCs and NPCs as good guys if there was more space for Utopians to continue working within the organization. From the defection of the Etherites and VAs and Navalon, and the comments of that ex-VE woman in Book of Worlds, it looks like you <i>can't</i> be a Utopian in the Union anymore, the same way you can't openly oppose the Communist Party in China. That would put Utopians in roughly the same powerless position as neonate vampires. They <i>can't </i>change the world or the Union, they can only defect and fight against it from outside it. And that constrains PC options.<br /> <br /> And unfortunately, since the Technocrats are also the main face of science, it also makes the whole game look anti-science. A nWoD fan friend of mine has zero interest in Ascension and Apocalypse because science is made to look so bad in both games. There are Etherites and Navalon, of course, but the Technocrats are much more prominently about SCIENCE (and Etherites look like pseudoscientist cooks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T22:59:10-08:00","id":1427248,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, Navalon is only a thing of you want it to be; if not, the Harbingers of Avalon are still within the ranks of the Union, giving the Utopians more of a place in its structure. In fact, they may still be there even if Navalon <i>is</i> a thing; one trend that the Disparate Alliance seems to feature is pocket groups within other factions such as the Bata'a faction within the Dreamspeakers or the Templar faction within the Celestial Chorus. Navalon might still have Harbingers of Avalon within the ranks of the Technocracy even as the new Craft seeks a place among the Disparates. <br /> <br /> That said, one reason I prefer the Navalon option is that Navalon has a chance to be in competition with the Union for the face of Science: unlike the Sons of Ether, their brand of Science (as I envision them) follows the same form and function as the Technocracy's; in M20 Focus terminology, they use the same Practices and Instruments. Even their Paradigms are quite similar, the key difference being what I outlined in my earlier post: Navalon is attempting to restore what it sees as the Craftsmasons' ideals (though given its name, it's <i>phrased</i> in terms of <i>Camelot's</i> ideals), with an ethical foundation to combat hubris. <br /> <br /> I'm still working on some of the details; but that's the gist of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-04-2020, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T23:32:28-08:00","id":1427249,"title":"","content":"I like the Traditions and the Disparate Alliance very much. I just also think there\u2019s good in everyone (except the Nephandi; Book of the Fallen REALLY creeped me out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T05:16:01-08:00","id":1427263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427241#post1427241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that as a splat design, it would be easier to depict Technocratic PCs and NPCs as good guys if there was more space for Utopians to continue working within the organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah<br /> <br /> I was a bit surprised they weren't mentioned more in latter books, because<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would put Utopians in roughly the same powerless position as neonate vampires. They <i>can't </i>change the world or the Union, they can only defect and fight against it from outside it. And that constrains PC options. </div> </div> </div>This shouldn't be the case after the Avatar Storm eliminated most of the leadership. At least in theory, it should be easier to get more power within the Union after Control was taken down.<br /> <br /> This was represented at some point with the Pogrom being called off, but I don't think it was mentioned much in the books - which focus more on the internal conflicts and dirty secrets between the Conventions.<br /> <br /> Still, the scenario of a potential technocratic civil war that was left before M20 it's a good opportunity, one would think, for change to happen from the inside and not just the outside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In fact, they may still be there even if Navalon <i>is</i> a thing; one trend that the Disparate Alliance seems to feature is pocket groups within other factions such as the Bata'a faction within the Dreamspeakers or the Templar faction within the Celestial Chorus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance was made by the Batini, it makes perfect sense for it to be subtle. Also because they don't have any chance of winning in a direct confrontation against any major faction. They should take advantage of the fact that they know how the system works to remain there, inflitrated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T05:42:47-08:00","id":1427265,"title":"","content":"Yeah; the reason why M20 refers to the Revised Convention Books as a \u201ckinder and gentler Technocracy\u201d is because they portrayed exactly this: the Union, separated from Control, got reorganized by the people on the ground; and in so doing, more room was made for those in its ranks that wanted to reform it.<br /> <br /> And the reason to have both the Harbingers of Avalon inside the Union and Navalon separate from it is that there are some things you can only do from the inside, and other things that you can only do from the outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-04-2020, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T06:10:25-08:00","id":1427267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427239#post1427239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Order of Reason did it first, but surely some of the Cult of Ecstasy worked very hard to make it so anyone can cook meth in their basement!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wise old stoner might be a stereotype now, but I'm pretty sure wise old meth head is a long way off. I don't think they've even achieved wise meth head or old meth head yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're absolutely right, but I don't think anyone's saying the average Technocrat gives a crap about commoners <i>anymore</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, capitalist was always completely elitist, with the &quot;common good&quot; as pure propaganda, but I can imagine that some Order of Reason ites (sp?) had honest populist intentions centuries before that. </div> </div> </div><br /> I may be in the minority but I think the typical Technocrat really does give a crap about the common man. The problem is many of them do so in the abstract. (Unsurprisingly, that's the same issue with their form of capitalism). They work towards the good of the teeming masses, but not the individuals in the teeming masses. No matter how populist and human centric any ideology risks becoming elitist when it treats people as numbers on a page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T14:10:55-08:00","id":1427299,"title":"","content":"I think CoE is more into stuff like DMT, LSD, psilocybin, cannabis, and other mind-altering stuff than meth. I'm sure some turn to stimulants but meth doesn't really seem to be an altered state of consciousness likely to lead to enlightenment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T16:12:07-08:00","id":1427312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427299#post1427299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think CoE is more into stuff like DMT, LSD, psilocybin, cannabis, and other mind-altering stuff than meth. I'm sure some turn to stimulants but meth doesn't really seem to be an altered state of consciousness likely to lead to enlightenment.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has tried a lot of amphetamine as well as some LSD, I have to say that from a simple perspective of getting an 'experiance' or interesting results from the usage, they can be compared. I can definitely imagine some CoE Mages going on night and day about the positives of going all speedy, and forgoing rest for extended periods of time. An intense stimulant high, especially when focused on distinct activities (PC games and listening to music in my case) is definitely a state of altered consciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-04-2020, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T16:49:11-08:00","id":1427314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427265#post1427265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; the reason why M20 refers to the Revised Convention Books as a \u201ckinder and gentler Technocracy\u201d is because they portrayed exactly this: the Union, separated from Control, got reorganized by the people on the ground; and in so doing, more room was made for those in its ranks that wanted to reform it.<br /> <br /> And the reason to have both the Harbingers of Avalon inside the Union and Navalon separate from it is that there are some things you can only do from the inside, and other things that you can only do from the outside.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The SYndicate and NWO conventions didn't seem THAT much Kinder. The Syndicate still came off in theirown book as solidly &quot;Working for the worst parts of the Status Quo&quot; Where as all the other conventions seemed to have a Utopian ideal to work towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T20:22:02-08:00","id":1427326,"title":"","content":"And not by coincidence: Syndicate and NWO are the two Conventions that were hit less by the Storm. They, especially the Syndicate, didn't lost so much of their leadership. That's why these two Conventions are the spear-heads of the civil war (that's universaly seen as something that would destroy the Union, if more level heads don't triumph)<br /> <br /> That being said, each book has a lot of things going on - and much isn't good. Like, at least the Syndicate doesn't see the benefit of restarting the Pogrom, while Progenitors are transiting a &quot;kill all the homeopats&quot; phase, and want to get back to it. All the Convention books (except the VE, I think. I don't remember it clearly) start with a fiction of technocrats doing something horrible, or at least moraly questionable<br /> <br /> VE seem to be the best of the bunch. They're an army now, but they're figthing the good figth, They have a new enemy that's undoubtedly dangerous (also ironical). Because they can't turn to the Technocracy against this threat, they're recruiting allies within the Traditions in order to fight it - opening a rare oportunity to make a sort of &quot;internal crossover&quot;, a PC party of both technocrats and traditions working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T21:29:11-08:00","id":1427330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427312#post1427312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who has tried a lot of amphetamine as well as some LSD, I have to say that from a simple perspective of getting an 'experiance' or interesting results from the usage, they can be compared. I can definitely imagine some CoE Mages going on night and day about the positives of going all speedy, and forgoing rest for extended periods of time. An intense stimulant high, especially when focused on distinct activities (PC games and listening to music in my case) is definitely a state of altered consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't mean to say that stimulants can't get a mind altering high. I have ADHD and have first-hand legal experience. What I should have said is that they'd be more likely to go for purer, less potentially harmful formulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T23:52:32-08:00","id":1427334,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in what people's thoughts of actual reform of the NWO and Syndicate would look like. That is, of you were to include a group (like Navalon, for instance) that uses the Practices and Instruments of these Conventions (so that you don't get the argument that \u201cthey're not really technologists\u201d that crops up so often for the Etherites) but changes the uses that those tools are put to so as to be something that's more of a positive, what would those changes look like? I have my own thoughts on what an <i>actually</i> \u201ckinder and gentler\u201d NWO and Syndicate would look like; but I want to hear others' thoughts first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T13:27:04-08:00","id":1427399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd be interested in what people's thoughts of actual reform of the NWO and Syndicate would look like. </div> </div> </div>Well, from the top of my head.<br /> <br /> NWO:<br /> Room 101 has to go. They need to be less trigger-happy with all that mind control. And allow people some privacy.<br /> Since they're the masters of social sciences: What if instead of making societies at their own image by testing &quot;perfect&quot; models in the Umbra, they start actually going to the living, breathing, societies and studying <i>what they want</i>?<br /> <br /> Syndicate:<br /> In your beloved status quo there are big amounts of people that live in practicaly medieval conditions - but with their ecosistems destroyed and the bad elements of their societies being armed with weapons far more destructive. So they actually live much worse.<br /> <br /> So, let's start from the Scarcity Problem - shall we: That cannot be treated as an unsolvable problem. Mages believing that a problem can't be solved (or that it's <i>incredibly hard</i> to solve) it's the same as them being <i>unable </i>to solve it. That force that prevent's people from flying it's <i>for sure </i>an Earthly Foundation, and that didn't stop ItX from making planes. Even when the first centuries they were <i>very </i>Vulgar. They're shooting themselves in the foot with those beliefs - unless their plan was to gain power for themselves at the expense of the majority (in that case a world defined by a savage competence for resources works perfectly).<br /> <br /> As the saying goes: Of course you can't, not with that attitude!<br /> <br /> Also <i>stop covering for Pentex</i> (I know they're no longer Pentex, but they still take their money and hidde their corruption).<br /> <br /> And stat taking charge of the fact your organization it's ruled by egoist assholes that need to be stopped. Yes, they are: The Syndicate literally has representatives of everything that's wrong in the world working for them: Crime lords, empresaries that use slave work, the international funds that crush countries with debt, weapon dealers, poluting compaines, the toxic advertising culture...etc. Representatives of ALL can be found working for the Syndicate! - all working in the name of defending the sacred rigth of &quot;the elites&quot; to enjoy the power they have <i>earned</i>, even if that power was <i>earned</i> making other people suffer.<br /> <br /> And, no, giving the Technocracy <i>moar </i>Quintessence/money so they can build <i>moar </i>killing devices doesn't justify any of this.<i> And even then that would be another lie of the Syndicate</i>, <i>because they enjoy this extra power themselves too. </i>So: police your damn people!, or we will have a hard time noticing the differences between you people and the money Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-05-2020, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T18:12:52-08:00","id":1427412,"title":"","content":"Scarcity isn't real. The enforcement of false scarcity is a critical part of capitalism, which the Syndicate promotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T14:29:13-08:00","id":1427492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427412#post1427412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scarcity isn't real. The enforcement of false scarcity is a critical part of capitalism, which the Syndicate promotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not so much a false problem as a problem of logistics that should have been solved by our <b>techno</b>logical development, but it wasn't thanks to how the Capitalism system - understood as more than just Liberalism, but as the way the superpowers that control humanity's vast resources interact in a worldwide scale - works.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I do think capitalism it's to blame. But this is a tricky subject, and you will see it if you bother to debate with any relatively smart libertarian - but I don't want to waste my time being the Devil's advocate here. Let's talk about the problem:<br /> <br /> As I understand this, it' s a problem of logistics: There's always food, and the stuff you need to live, on the planet - somewhere. But sometimes it's winter where you are, plant's die, animals that eat plants die, and there's no food where you are - hence the scarcity. This is a problem that long predates Capitalism.<br /> <br /> Now, our <b>techno</b>logical advancements allow us to have food all the year, everywhere, and in suchn quantities that it would be enough for <i>everyone</i>. But, of course, this is not God given, this costs energy - understood as fuel and also human resources. <i>The System </i>(Capitalism, understood as a global phenomena) <i>manages</i> this energy.<br /> In our current global society, all this energy it's moved by the desire of individuals to get richer - hence the problem: It's never going to be proffitable to give stuff to the people in need, you take the bother to move all that energy and human resources to give the stuff to the people that can <i>pay </i>(which historically are always going to be the people that won wars - phisical, comercial or otherwise - in the past, and got all the loot and the rigths).<br /> <br /> Now, I've higligthed the word <b>techno </b>- because in our world scarcity would not be possible to solve without technology- And , in fact, it's only imaginable to solve it trough it. Otherwise winter (to put an example - also plagues, drougths, etc. You know) it's always going to kill your food unless you live on one of those rare paradices of abundance where that never happens. The fact that hungers always existed should be proof enough that scarcity wasn't invented by Capitalism<br /> <br /> In WoD the Technocracy made possible for us to imagine the defeat of scarcity, by employing human resources to trasport food and other basics to everyone. But what if other, mystical, Mage factions made it possible? - Energy &amp; human resources are ultimately represented by Quintessence and Will/Arete. So, it would be disingenuous to think a mystical paradigm would't need to <i>face it as a</i> <i>real problem - </i>before solving it with magick. In order to solve this problem you need a way to <i>administer </i>this energy that's not based so much arround the desire of egoist material gain...<br /> <br /> And, yeah, the Syndicate's Paradigm it's based arround the kind of egoism that justifies the way the system works - so maybe they're to blame for the <i>demonstrated lack of capacity </i>of the Technocracy to end scarcity (also they killed the only ones that wanted to do so). But they say this is a natural law, like an Eartly Foundation. People just works like that, and they have to work arround this fact.<br /> <br /> This may be wrong, or even a lie - BUT I'm willing to entertain the posibility it is a Foundation because I think that the best way to demolish someone's argument forever it's if you can <b>face them at their best</b>. I say: Even if it was a Foundation, by believing that this human problem can't be solved you're weakening your own magick. It may be necessary to make some workarrounds to solve Scarcity, if it's such a thing, but you still need a firm Will to do whatever it's necessary to defeat it, if you want ever be able to<i> - at least</i> - make things better for most people. By defending the status quo, and the privileges of the elite, they're defending scarcity too. Even if it was a real problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-06-2020, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T19:19:31-08:00","id":1427510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427492#post1427492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's not so much a false problem as a problem of logistics that should have been solved by our <b>techno</b>logical development, but it wasn't thanks to how the Capitalism system - understood as more than just Liberalism, but as the way the superpowers that control humanity's vast resources interact in a worldwide scale - works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Capitalism plays a huge role in this, and it's weird that anyone could think otherwise. We produce more food than anyone could eat, and so much of it gets thrown away. We have an overproduction problem and you would see it if you bother to debate with any informed socialist.<br /> <br /> Capitalism plays a significant role in where commodities are distributed. Which is to say, they're distributed where there's money, and often produced where it's cheapest to produce. Which is to say corporations gravitate to places where they can pay workers pennies on the dollar while collective massive amounts of money on the results of their labor. Since these places are poor it's not very profitable to distribute commodities there - instead they get distributed where people will pay for them. And even then, overproduction means that a significant amount of these commodities don't get sold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427492#post1427492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, I do think capitalism it's to blame. But this is a tricky subject, and you will see it if you bother to debate with any relatively smart libertarian</div> </div> </div> </div>Libertarians are hampered by committing themselves to a flawed ideology that won't work out the way they think it will. One needs only look at Paul Ryan's record as Speaker of the House to see how applied libertarianism actually further restricts the distribution of resources, and mostly restricts it from the poorest people.<br /> <br /> An &quot;intelligent libertarian&quot; is in it to get rich, not to improve society. The most intelligent libertarian understands that only a few people have any chance of acquiring serious wealth. Anything they say will be geared toward their own self interest, and can thus be discarded as heavily biased. A truly intelligent libertarian would see the ideology as the cannibalistic con job that it is and get out.<br /> <br /> Barely restrained capitalism is destroying the environment and killing people. There's no valid defense for it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T23:39:36-08:00","id":1427526,"title":"","content":"Damn, is most of the Mage fanbase Technocracy apologists? What's the point of calling it Mage when most of the fanbase for this line is purely enamored with the Men-in-Black Totally Not Mages and Not the Bad Guys @TM part of it.. that decidedly don't count themselves as Mages and all their &quot;magick&quot; (well the quotations are dubious because what they do IS magick, but they claim it isn't- but that's beside the point) is merely &quot;high-technology&quot;... I always found it bizarre that they would be more popular than the Traditions and the Disparates..<br /> <br /> EDIT: But who am I kidding; I even pointed this out before. Way too much attention is developed onto the Technocracy and no other faction in the Mage gameline. For pete-sake, they're making a whole new M20 book for the Technocracy, but none of the other factions.. at all. How did it up like this for Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T02:11:07-08:00","id":1427538,"title":"","content":"Mage had two tradition books for every tradition and multiple other books that developed the Traditions further. There isn't a lack of stuff for the Council of Nine.<br /> <br /> Would love to see a book for the Traditions and Disparates each, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T04:46:54-08:00","id":1427562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427526#post1427526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, is most of the Mage fanbase Technocracy apologists? What's the point of calling it Mage when most of the fanbase for this line is purely enamored with the Men-in-Black Totally Not Mages and Not the Bad Guys @TM part of it.. that decidedly don't count themselves as Mages and all their &quot;magick&quot; (well the quotations are dubious because what they do IS magick, but they claim it isn't- but that's beside the point) is merely &quot;high-technology&quot;... I always found it bizarre that they would be more popular than the Traditions and the Disparates..<br /> <br /> EDIT: But who am I kidding; I even pointed this out before. Way too much attention is developed onto the Technocracy and no other faction in the Mage gameline. For pete-sake, they're making a whole new M20 book for the Technocracy, but none of the other factions.. at all. How did it up like this for Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>First edition had 15 supplements; 3 were devoted to the Technocracy (Iteration X, Progenitors, NWO), 3 to Technomancers (Digital Web, VAs, and Sons of Ether), and 2 to mystical Traditions (Verbena and Akashic Brotherhood). <br /> <br /> Second Edition had 21 supplements; 3 were devoted to the Technocracy (Void Engineers, Syndicate, and Guide to the Technocracy), 2 were devoted to Technomancers (Digital Web 2.0 and Technomancers Toybox), 5 to Traditions, and 1 to Disparates (the Book of Crafts). <br /> <br /> Revised Edition had 30 supplements, including 5 Convention Books (4 of which were published a decade later), 2 Technomancer books (the revised VA and Etherite Tradition Books), and 8 Tradition Books (including the Guide to the Traditions). 5 books could kinda sorta be seen as Disparate books if you squint (Dead Magic I and II, Dragons of the East, Lost Paths, and Hollow Ones), but MRev was big on the notion of eliminating the Crafts as something separate, for the most part opting to fold them into the Traditions. <br /> <br /> All told: from 1993 to 2004, the Technocracy got 7 books (five \u201cConvention Books\u201d, the Guide to the Technocracy, and one Revised Convention Book), while the Traditions got 19 or 20 (the original 9 Tradition Books, the Guide to the Traditions, and 9 or 10 revised Tradition Books, depending on how you count the Hollow Ones) and the Disparates got upward of 5 or 6, despite being given the shaft throughout most of that period. If you include everything up to the year before M20 came out, that count for the Technocracy bumps up to 11; still far short of what the Traditions got. <br /> <br /> M20 doesn't yet have any books out for the Technocracy, though it's going to have one (Technocracy Reloaded) and one Technomancer book (TR's companion book). Granted, there aren't going to be equivalent books about the Traditions or the Disparates; but that's not out of a lack of desire to do them: everything that's currently in the pipeline for Mage has been in there for a while, and it appears that the new White Wolf hasn't been authorizing anything new. In particular, Brucato wanted to do a Disparate Alliance book, but was shot down by White Wolf. Basically, it looks right now like M20 is on its last gasp publication-wise as White Wolf is looking to clear the decks for M5.<br /> <br /> Heck, even the fact that TR got a Kickstarter could be viewed as Onyx Path attempting to breathe some life into the M20 publication line, as opposed to being about wanting to single out the Technocracy as more important than anyone else. From what I understand, Victorian Mage will be getting a similar treatment. <br /> <br /> As for the fanbase: don't confuse a vocal minority for a majority. Conversely, note that for the most part, the closest thing to a defense of the Technocracy has been \u201cshades of gray\u201d, not \u201cTechnocrats are the good guys\u201d. There has been <i>one post</i> of the latter here, and a broad consensus that there's no merit to that claim. <br /> <br /> Finally: if you don't like how much oxygen this is getting, <i>stop giving it oxygen</i>. It's perfectly valid to simply ignore a thread that you don't like. It's also perfectly valid to start or participate in other threads that are more to your liking. One of the more troubling things in recent years has been this notion that \u201cif I don't like it, then nobody should talk about it\u201d; and I'm glad that the Onyx Path forums have largely avoided that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-07-2020, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T08:20:11-08:00","id":1427596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427510#post1427510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Capitalism plays a huge role in this, and it's weird that anyone could think otherwise. We produce more food than anyone could eat, and so much of it gets thrown away. We have an overproduction problem and you would see it if you bother to debate with any informed socialist.<br /> <br /> Capitalism plays a significant role in where commodities are distributed. Which is to say, they're distributed where there's money, and often produced where it's cheapest to produce. Which is to say corporations gravitate to places where they can pay workers pennies on the dollar while collective massive amounts of money on the results of their labor. Since these places are poor it's not very profitable to distribute commodities there - instead they get distributed where people will pay for them. And even then, overproduction means that a significant amount of these commodities don't get sold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've used this combination in the past but two of the great Technocrat inspirations are Norman Borlaug and Trofim Lysenko; technology and ideology at their best and worst.. Norman Borlaug can reasonably be credited with saving billions of people from starvation through modern science, the resources of developed nations, and humanitarian aid, and he specifically focused on areas with poor food production.. Trofim Lysenko was responsible for the starvation of millions by spreading a Lamarkian theory of genetics within the USSR and using his connections to have rivals executed. Borlaug's efforts are inseparable from Capitalism, but clearly rise beyond the economic system. Lysenko's efforts are inseparable from Marxism (he specifically called his rivals enemies of Marxism) and he dragged everything else down to that level. One used science and money in the advancement of human dignity, the other shackled science and supply chains in the name of ideological suitability.<br /> <br /> This being Mage, the Technocracy (or any group trying to replace it) has to have both. It is important to feed and shelter people and protect them from monsters in the dark. It is also important that the right cause (and for that matter, the right Cause) get the credit for achievements because that is part of how people accept it as right. Yes, they can save a lot more people now, but if they do it the wrong way will they be able to save them tomorrow? It actually doesn't matter what the ideology or paradigm is, if there is a Borlaug to admire, there is a Lysenko waiting in the shadows. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427510#post1427510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An &quot;intelligent libertarian&quot; is in it to get rich, not to improve society. The most intelligent libertarian understands that only a few people have any chance of acquiring serious wealth. Anything they say will be geared toward their own self interest, and can thus be discarded as heavily biased. A truly intelligent libertarian would see the ideology as the cannibalistic con job that it is and get out.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a description of Libertarianism that's remarkably simplistic and one-dimensional. I don't think you managed to reference any of the core elements of the philosophy. It's not really relevant to Mage, though, so I won't comment further on the subject.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T08:57:38-08:00","id":1427598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally: if you don't like how much oxygen this is getting, stop giving it oxygen. It's perfectly valid to simply ignore a thread that you don't like. It's also perfectly valid to start or participate in other threads that are more to your liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, the whole point of forums is the discussion of things. I go into threads with subjects that interest me; whether or not its something that I don't like or like. Like the discussion of Obtenebration and its relation to the cosmology of oWoD; or when I talked about the Tzimisce's relation to their Path of Metamorphosis weeks ago in another thread. The topic centering around the pivot of the Mage fanbase toward the Technocracy is something that amuses me. And to note; I have ignored threads centering around topics that haven't interested me and something I didn't like as well before. If no one talked on forums it would be dead- which is very easy for Onyx considering how slow it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the more troubling things in recent years has been this notion that \u201cif I don't like it, then nobody should talk about it\u201d; and I'm glad that the Onyx Path forums have largely avoided that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet we're all still talking about the subject matter, aren't we?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, even the fact that TR got a Kickstarter could be viewed as Onyx Path attempting to breathe some life into the M20 publication line, as opposed to being about wanting to single out the Technocracy as more important than anyone else. From what I understand, Victorian Mage will be getting a similar treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>If its said that everything is still in the pipeline of development things were cleared to wait for M5, how come the Technocracy of all things had gotten chosen for one last M20 output? And why would they make a Victorian setting book instead of doing a Traditions book to swing along with the Technology Reloaded and Technomancer book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:59:10-08:00","id":1427608,"title":"","content":"Those decisions were made years ago when the environment was different. I have no doubt that the original plan was to release the key core books first (that is, <b>HDYDT</b>, [b]Book of Secrets [/by, and <b>Gods and Monsters</b>, which together consist of \u201cmost of what Brucato wanted to put into M20, but couldn't find the room\u201d), followed by faction-oriented books written in the order of most needed to least needed (where the ranking was according to Brucato's judgment of needs), and a number of other projects that the Mage team has always wanted to write but never quite got around to interspersed. Thus, <b>Victorian Mage</b> and the supplement about money magic, the name of which currently escapes me. <br /> <br /> In terms of the faction books, here's what I think was the rationale for each: <br /> <br /> <b>Book of the Fallen</b> goes first, because the existing material on the Nephandi is limited to just the two editions of the <b>Book of Madness</b>, both of which are too \u201ccomic book evil\u201d for Brucato's liking. That needed to be rectified ASAP, so it went first. <br /> <br /> <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> came next because while there was a significant body of material available for Technocrats, most of it was getting increasingly outdated (everything but the last four Convention Books) and/or didn't align all that well with M20. <br /> <br /> The Disparates were going to be next, because they desperately needed more material. I think the only reason why the Technocracy went first was because the Technocrats are one of the more visible factions in the game while the Disparates are largely hidden. <br /> <br /> By contrast, the Traditions went last because, well, there are already 19 books written specifically about them; and unlike the Technocracy stuff, that material isn't particularly problematic. I'm sure they would have gotten an M20 supplement eventually; but there just want as much urgency for such as the was for the other factions. <br /> <br /> Heck, for all I know the M20 version of <b>Guide to the Traditions</b> likely would have come out after the M20 edition of the <b>Book of Madness</b> (which Phil has days that he wanted to do just as soon as he could figure out how to do it properly). <br /> <br /> The problem is that the last three of these (Disparates, Traditions, and Marauders) weren't in the pipeline when White Wolf decided to stop authorizing new X20 material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T17:38:44-08:00","id":1427653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427596#post1427596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I've used this combination in the past but two of the great Technocrat inspirations are Norman Borlaug and Trofim Lysenko; technology and ideology at their best and worst.. Norman Borlaug can reasonably be credited with saving billions of people from starvation through modern science, the resources of developed nations, and humanitarian aid, and he specifically focused on areas with poor food production.. Trofim Lysenko was responsible for the starvation of millions by spreading a Lamarkian theory of genetics within the USSR and using his connections to have rivals executed. Borlaug's efforts are inseparable from Capitalism, but clearly rise beyond the economic system. Lysenko's efforts are inseparable from Marxism (he specifically called his rivals enemies of Marxism) and he dragged everything else down to that level. One used science and money in the advancement of human dignity, the other shackled science and supply chains in the name of ideological suitability.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was a Marxist-Leninist, which is a tendency distinct from Marxism itself. Marxism or Marxist-Leninism doesn't lend itself to pseudoscience, that is something people tend to do, and far more and often much more harmful pseudoscience has been spread under capitalism for decades. Lysenko calling his enemies enemies of Marxism does not in fact make what he did actually Marxist, or even Marxist-Leninist.<br /> <br /> I would in fact go so far as to say Shell's and Exxon's suppression of research demonstrating and predicting global warming in the 80s has already done far more harm than Lysenko ever could have, and will do an order of magnitude more harm at least than it already has. And this is a strictly capitalist problem in that these corporations did it so they could continue to profitably extract and sell petroleum products and not have to spend more money developing cleaner energy sources.<br /> <br /> How about insulin? Insulin prices are extremely high in the US, and it's not nearly that expensive to produce. Pharmaceutical corporations that produce insulin understand that diabetic people have no choice but to get insulin or die, or at least suffer. Under capitalism, it &quot;makes sense&quot; for price gouging because these people can't really go anywhere else for this product.<br /> <br /> Lysenko was a problem, but not a uniquely <i>Marxist</i> problem. Shell and Exxon are uniquely capitalist problems. Insulin prices are a uniquely Borlaug's actions are not uniquely capitalist, and China has raised far more people out of poverty than Capitalism ever has. I'm not a fan of China, but presenting two examples is necessarily limited.<br /> <br /> Under capitalism, there is an even greater potential motivation for someone like Lysenko to try to exploit the system because there's money it for them if they succeed. And I already named one of the examples (Exxon + Shell and global warming), but there's also the tobacco industry's attempts to undercut evidence that smoking cigarettes is harmful to one's health. Wherever there's money to be made or a cash flow to maintain, there's a motivation to present a distorted version of reality to keep that money coming in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427596#post1427596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This being Mage, the Technocracy (or any group trying to replace it) has to have both. It is important to feed and shelter people and protect them from monsters in the dark. It is also important that the right cause (and for that matter, the right Cause) get the credit for achievements because that is part of how people accept it as right. Yes, they can save a lot more people now, but if they do it the wrong way will they be able to save them tomorrow? It actually doesn't matter what the ideology or paradigm is, if there is a Borlaug to admire, there is a Lysenko waiting in the shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any analysis of the Technocracy's actions needs to take them as a whole, throughout the time they've existed. One can't simply say &quot;well sure, Technocrats have done bad things, but there's always someone willing to do good stuff.&quot; Of course there is! But colonialism is an ongoing problem in which capitalist exploitation of developing nations is definitely a thing that the Technocracy is up to their elbows in and has been all along. As is global warming, as is income inequality. The world the Technocracy as an institution has participated in creating is not good. A &quot;Borlaug&quot; here or there doesn't mitigate that fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427596#post1427596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a description of Libertarianism that's remarkably simplistic and one-dimensional. I don't think you managed to reference any of the core elements of the philosophy. It's not really relevant to Mage, though, so I won't comment further on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care about the philosophy, what they <i>say</i> they believe. I care about the results of implementing their policies, which are uniformly harmful to everyone but the wealthiest people. Libertarianism as a political philosophy and practice, does not lead to any kind of common good. It leads to poverty, wage slavery, corporate underregulation, and rapacious exploitation. Ending government inspection of food production in the US this past year, for example, is something Libertarians want, and like. And also it leads to food poisoning and already has with deli meats (listeria) on the east coast. It leads to privatization of police and fire.<br /> <br /> Also, it's really weird for you to complain I didn't adequately discuss the extremely selfish philosophy Libertarians aspire to when you declared Lysenkoism is a Marxist problem because Lysenko said his enemies were enemies of Marxism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T05:21:03-08:00","id":1427699,"title":"","content":"You are spending an awful lot of time defending against arguments I did not make. Nor are any of your examples condemnations of capitalism but of people exploiting the strange interface between capitalism and government control (and to be clear, that's not an endorsement of pure capitalism, which has its own failings that said control is there to ward against).<br /> <br /> I'd address it more if I could see a way of applying it to the Traditions or Technocracy. I suppose maybe the conflict between the NWO and Syndicate, but that's a reach...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427653#post1427653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He was a Marxist-Leninist, which is a tendency distinct from Marxism itself. Marxism or Marxist-Leninism doesn't lend itself to pseudoscience, that is something people tend to do, and far more and often much more harmful pseudoscience has been spread under capitalism for decades. Lysenko calling his enemies enemies of Marxism does not in fact make what he did actually Marxist, or even Marxist-Leninist.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Lysenko was a problem, but not a uniquely <i>Marxist</i> problem. Shell and Exxon are uniquely capitalist problems. Insulin prices are a uniquely Borlaug's actions are not uniquely capitalist, and China has raised far more people out of poverty than Capitalism ever has. I'm not a fan of China, but presenting two examples is necessarily limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed it but that was my point. These achievements and these excesses come from humanity; its virtues and its vices. The political/economic system does not make them more or less likely to happen, it merely changes the opportunities for their expression. Lysenko could only have rivals executed in a system where it was possible to have rivals executed, but that doesn't mean he couldn't have leveraged his influence to shut out rivals in another system. He was not an example of science slaved to marxism but of science slaved to what was politically correct (not in the modern sense of the term but what was actually politically allowable in his time).<br /> <br /> That's the meaning behind the Technocracy having a Lysenko waiting in the shadows. It doesn't mean they are always in danger of turning Marxist, that would be a rather silly claim. It means that they always have a motivation to suppress doing good if it is not good in the right way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any analysis of the Technocracy's actions needs to take them as a whole, throughout the time they've existed. One can't simply say &quot;well sure, Technocrats have done bad things, but there's always someone willing to do good stuff.&quot; Of course there is! But colonialism is an ongoing problem in which capitalist exploitation of developing nations is definitely a thing that the Technocracy is up to their elbows in and has been all along. As is global warming, as is income inequality. The world the Technocracy as an institution has participated in creating is not good. A &quot;Borlaug&quot; here or there doesn't mitigate that fact. </div> </div> </div>Hence pairing Borlaug with Lysenko. You can't ignore either of them, they are both representative of the Technocracy. Borlaug as what it strives to be, Lysenko as what it is willing to do. The Technocracy has in many ways created a golden age where people in the lowest income live with luxuries that kings couldn't have two hundred years ago, and in doing so they've opened the door (or actively created) dehumanizing and oppressive systems and practices. The benefits surely don't eclipse the costs, but neither do the costs invalidate the benefits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't care about the philosophy, what they <i>say</i> they believe. I care about the results of implementing their policies, which are uniformly harmful to everyone but the wealthiest people. Libertarianism as a political philosophy and practice, does not lead to any kind of common good. It leads to poverty, wage slavery, corporate underregulation, and rapacious exploitation. Ending government inspection of food production in the US this past year, for example, is something Libertarians want, and like. And also it leads to food poisoning and already has with deli meats (listeria) on the east coast. It leads to privatization of police and fire. </div> </div> </div>Well if I'm not going to discuss the political stance of Libertarians here, I'm certainly not going to discuss your perceptions and stereotypes about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 12-08-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T07:43:05-08:00","id":1427705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427412#post1427412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scarcity isn't real. The enforcement of false scarcity is a critical part of capitalism, which the Syndicate promotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If scarcity isn't real and is enforced by the Syndicate, then why was there scarcity before even the Technocracy was conceived of and the order of reason formed?<br /> <br /> If scarcity was invented by the Syndicate, why can't the Traditions reject it and create infinite amounts of Primium and Quintessence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T08:24:54-08:00","id":1427712,"title":"","content":"Of course scarcity is real. The argument that Resplendent Fire is referring to is that a lot of what's <i>called</i> scarcity arguably isn't. For instance, food: large portions of the world's population are starving; but that isn't because there isn't enough food to go around, it's because the food is concentrated in certain parts of the world (like North America) and isn't distributed freely to the rest of it. The problem here isn't scarcity; it's distribution. <br /> <br /> And where Syndicate upper management falls down is that it <i>is</i> \u201cbottom line <i>uber alles</i>: because they view everything <i>strictly</i> through the lens of profit, they're not going to do anything that isn't profitable. <br /> <br /> It's a rather short-sighted perspective, and an overly simplified one. A less corrupt version of or alternative to the Syndicate would temper the profit motive. For example, there's philanthropy, where rich people spend money on charity. A Syndicate variant that practices and encourages that would be a lot less problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-08-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T09:45:47-08:00","id":1427721,"title":"","content":"On the NWO, I generally agree with what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said on the matter; but I'd like to elaborate a bit. It's not just room 101 that has to go. It's Conditioning. Technocracy Reloaded compares the Union to a cult, and Conditioning is a big part of why. NWO's willingness to use mind control at the drop of a hat is a manifestation of the aforementioned control freakery of the Union, filtered through the fact that they are the Convention that deals with Mind: one of the main things that Mind lets you do is mind control. That's an awfully big temptation. So what a variant NWO needs is something to counter that temptation. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar896_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"896\" data-vbnamecard=\"896\">Erinys</a> mentioned earlier that Technocrats are just as likely as Sleepers to be stupid, destructive, and corrupt; I agree, which is why an NWO variant needs to be more concerned with tracking, learning, and communication than with manipulation and control: it's all too easy to fall into the trap of thinking that you know better. <br /> <br /> Heck, even with that, you need to be careful of the very fine line that exists between education and indoctrination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:11:45-08:00","id":1427722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a rather short-sighted perspective, and an overly simplified one. A less corrupt certain of our alternative to the Syndicate would temper the profit motive. For example, there's philanthropy, where rich people spend money on charity. A Syndicate variant that practices and encourages that would be a lot less problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>And like Resplendent Fire mentioned before, there is some room for &quot;good&quot; in the Technocracy, but it isn't the norm. Most of it is plain ambivalence, questionable acts, and straight evil ones. The cusp of the Consensus of oWoD is apparently in their hands and they literally can sway reality to what they want, but oWoD as a universe is somehow shittier than our own even with the advantages they have. The Traditions (who they claim were the cause for humanities &quot;sufferings&quot;) as is practically aren't a threat and have been literally destroyed by the Technocracy multiple times in MTA lore. So what gives? <br /> <br /> &quot;A less corrupt certain of our alternative to the Syndicate&quot; is merely a what-if. This section of the Technocracy has practically ruled it de-facto since its start as the High Guild and later on to its current namesake. It has dealt everything with the concern for profit only and nothing else nor does the Syndicate as a whole care about the common man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:59:51-08:00","id":1427730,"title":"","content":"You may not have noticed, but I have been spitballing ideas about Navalon. You know: \u201ca breakaway group of idealistic Technocrats who revere the example of King Arthur and despise the corruption of their former Union\u201d (M20, p.200). That's what my \u201cless corrupt version of or alternative to\u201d comment was mostly about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T12:21:43-08:00","id":1427735,"title":"","content":"Oh, I got confused because people in this thread said Navalon were remnants of the Craftmasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T12:31:29-08:00","id":1427737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427722#post1427722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And like Resplendent Fire mentioned before, there is some room for &quot;good&quot; in the Technocracy, but it isn't the norm. Most of it is plain ambivalence, questionable acts, and straight evil ones. The cusp of the Consensus of oWoD is apparently in their hands and they literally can sway reality to what they want, but oWoD as a universe is somehow shittier than our own even with the advantages they have. The Traditions (who they claim were the cause for humanities &quot;sufferings&quot;) as is practically aren't a threat and have been literally destroyed by the Technocracy multiple times in MTA lore. So what gives?<br /> <br /> &quot;A less corrupt certain of our alternative to the Syndicate&quot; is merely a what-if. This section of the Technocracy has practically ruled it de-facto since its start as the High Guild and later on to its current namesake. It has dealt everything with the concern for profit only and nothing else nor does the Syndicate as a whole care about the common man.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the ways I picture the differences between the NWO and the Syndicate is the way they see regular people and the specific ways they dehumanize them. <br /> <br /> To my mind, the NWO is more likely to care about the human story. They are more likely to see individuals as individuals and more likely to look for anecdotes to put human faces to triumphs and tragedies. The flip side of this is that they are prone to making gross assumptions about what people want and generalizing from specific examples. They are also much more prone to solutions that rely on perfecting people or consigning people to the dustbin of history. When they misjudge people, it is the people who are wrong. <br /> <br /> The Syndicate on the other hand is much more accepting of people as they are. They seek to perfect systems not individuals. That said they also much more likely to view people as numbers on a page. They'll do the market research to find out what is important to people and miss the why. They are prone to missing the consequences of their actions through their distance.<br /> <br /> The NWO cares very much about the common man, so long as they get to choose who the common man is. The Syndicate cares very much about the common man as represented by numbers on a spreadsheet.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T12:48:55-08:00","id":1427740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427735#post1427735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I got confused because people in this thread said Navalon were remnants of the Craftmasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that I see Navalon as the spiritual heirs to the Craftmasons. And I also said that I see the Craftmasons as the conscience of the Order of Reason; the two statements should be taken as a set, as in \u201cI view Navalon as what the Technocracy would be like if it hadn't lost its way\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-08-2020, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T06:29:31-08:00","id":1429849,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Lysenkoism have worked in the USSR given how Mage metaphysics work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T08:39:30-08:00","id":1429864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1429849#post1429849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Lysenkoism have worked in the USSR given how Mage metaphysics work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This really has nothing to do with the topic, especially given that in the WoD it was the <i>Etherites</i> who were the most prominent Mage faction behind the early USSR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T09:25:19-08:00","id":1429870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1429849#post1429849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Lysenkoism have worked in the USSR given how Mage metaphysics work?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like to cite Climate Change denial as my go-to example of why there needs to be more to the nature of reality than just \u201cwhatever the Consensus says\u201d, this also illustrates the same point. You can't get rid of Climate Change by making the Consensus \u201cdisbelieve\u201d it, and you can't cause Lysenkoism to <i>work</i> by making the Consensus believe it. In both cases, what you end up with is a Consensus that's in Denial. It takes something else besides merely shifting the Consensus to make real, lasting change to the Tapestry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T16:10:37-08:00","id":1429907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1429870#post1429870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like to cite Climate Change denial as my go-to example of why there needs to be more to the nature of reality than just \u201cwhatever the Consensus says\u201d, this also illustrates the same point. You can't get rid of Climate Change by making the Consensus \u201cdisbelieve\u201d it, and you can't cause Lysenkoism to <i>work</i> by making the Consensus believe it. In both cases, what you end up with is a Consensus that's in Denial. It takes something else besides merely shifting the Consensus to make real, lasting change to the Tapestry.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is that something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T00:11:04-08:00","id":1429923,"title":"","content":"Was Lysenkoism ever THAT widely believed on?<br /> <br /> Because the mention that Lysenko had to accuse people of being anty-comunist (get them into trouble) to do his things suggests to me that there were people who didn't believe so much.<br /> <br /> Maybe dissidents were a minority here, people believed enthusiastically and it should have worked. <hr /><br /> Let's entertain the notion that it should have worked. Disclaimer: It's all game theory here, there's no final answer from the &quot;Mage metaphysics&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, the Consensus it's the power of ALL Avatars to alter reality in accordance to human belief and will. If you believe in forces that exist beyond human belief, then the Consensus simply was blocked by those outside powers.<br /> <br /> I think you could imagine altering reality as a ritual where you want the largest amount of participats to add to the power of the ritual, and the least amount of complications that could make it fail.<br /> <br /> So, you have to:<br /> *Convince more people to increase the power of such beliefs in the Consensus and decrease the power of the beliefs working against you<br /> *Do some work arround that produces the desired result yet finds less resistance from the outside forces. People can't fly, but maybe there are times where they can. Loads of stuff fly. Find a &quot;bug&quot; or something to cheat the universe into believing that your stuff maybe should fly, so it becomes less salty about it.<br /> <br /> There's another dial: Increasing the power of that which comprises the Consensus. Awakened Avatars have a greater influence on Reality than sleepers (sleepers only rule the Consensus because they have a tremendous numerical advantage). It stands to reason that more Awakened would increase the power of humanity to change the Tapestry. Mass Awakening migth be powerful enough to overwhelm any outside opposition. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-26-2020, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:08:08-08:00","id":1429970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1429849#post1429849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Lysenkoism have worked in the USSR given how Mage metaphysics work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. If the Lysenko\u2019s methods worked the Technocracy would have won already. Unfortunately for them, human reaction and belief is difficult to predict. <br /> <br /> Look at it this way, through control of the media and journals Lysenko could convince the cities and the universities (somewhat) but that\u2019s not where the food was grown. For the farmers he was just forcing them to do something they didn\u2019t think would work. No surprise then that it didn\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:40:59-08:00","id":1429972,"title":"","content":"M20's balkanized Consensus (i.e., Reality Zones) does help here, in that the beliefs of the city-dwelling technocrats (note the lower-case) don't hold much sway over the more rural regions, especially in an era before the rise of mass communications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T10:08:54-08:00","id":1430095,"title":"","content":"If I remember right, there's a line of historical thinking that Lysenko was successful in part because he <i>did</i> actually have a lot of success gaining the trust of peasants. He was a comparatively self-educated peasant with his own relatively common sense ideas about agronomy (even if they were wrong), whilst Vavilov and co were the big city guys, who also had a bad habit of overpromising. In the context of the collectivisation, dekulakisation, and the Holodomor; the Soviet state really needed someone to rebuild trust with the peasantry, which in this case was Lysenko.<br /> <br /> However, if we want to keep to Mage metaphysics though; consider that the Soviet agricultural sector in general still significantly underperformed for pretty much all of it's existence. That wasn't the product of Lysenkoism, it was a product of treating the peasantry really badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T14:38:45-08:00","id":1430500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427100#post1427100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, I absolutely agree with. Well, with the exception of the Nephandi. <i>They</i> are absolute jack holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this as a major problem with all editions of M:tAs. The game talks about how belief creates truth, but it contains more pre-packaged truths I could easily count. One of them is that there is a faction that is Inherently Evil and metaphysically recognized by everyone as being enemies. If you look at what M20 initially uses to describe them, they could include character concepts in which they're like the Euthanatoi but for the cosmos rather than individual things within it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26588-melendwyr","name":"Melendwyr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T18:37:56-08:00","id":1430519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melendwyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430500#post1430500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game talks about how belief creates truth, but it contains more pre-packaged truths I could easily count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Belief shaping reality isn't exactly the same as creating truth. But split hairs aside, that's one reason more to believe Mage isn't absolutely relativistic, that there *is* a world outside the dreams of humanity after all.<br /> <br /> Really, Mage never goes so far. If *<i>everything</i>* depends uppon the Consensus, that calls for troublesome questions like &quot;then how did humans came to be?&quot;. Also Mage has stories about the origin of the universe, and the origin of magick, that talk about inhuman forces other than &quot;the Consensus&quot; (The One, The Pures). These could be false, but also could be rigth - and if one believes they hold truth, then there's a lot of objective in the cosmos.<br /> <br /> But <i>belief </i><i>shaping </i><i>reality </i>can still be true. Your hands can shape clay, but that doesn't mean you made the clay. Ultimately, it's up to the ST to define *how much* does belief change the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-30-2020, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T20:05:35-08:00","id":1430531,"title":"","content":"Yeah; one problem with going fully relativistic is that \u201c100% of all statistics are wrong.\u201d Go with a fully subjective reality, and nothing can be absolutely true \u2014 including the fact that nothing is absolutely true. Paradox. <br /> <br /> By the way, welcome to the forum, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26588-melendwyr\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26588\" data-vbnamecard=\"26588\">Melendwyr</a>! I'll note, in your defense, that you're not the only one who would prefer the Nephandi to have some sort of redeeming element buried somewhere in their philosophy. Not <i>me</i>, mind you; I'm fine with the Nephandi as they're presented in <b>Book of the Fallen</b>. But there are a few here who share your opinion. I'll see if I can dig up one of the threads that addressed the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T07:05:45-08:00","id":1430564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melendwyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430500#post1430500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see this as a major problem with all editions of M:tAs. The game talks about how belief creates truth, but it contains more pre-packaged truths I could easily count. One of them is that there is a faction that is Inherently Evil and metaphysically recognized by everyone as being enemies. If you look at what M20 initially uses to describe them, they could include character concepts in which they're like the Euthanatoi but for the cosmos rather than individual things within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might help you to consider the Nephandi as irreconcilably alien rather than irredeemably evil. From the outside they appear evil, that might not be the case from the inside. Mages can\u2019t know that without becoming one and that\u2019s a one way trip.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the thing with the Nephandi, they are the absolute that proves the reletavistic rule. While everyone else is arguing that morality might be subjective, they are the ones which show it may be very real. In many ways the Technocracy and Traditions can get so lost in the philosophical arguments that they (and we) lose track of the real weight of what they are doing, that can\u2019t happen with the Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T07:52:43-08:00","id":1430568,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that \u201cirreconcilably alien\u201d is a better fit for the Marauders than the Nephandi. Part of what makes the Nephandi so insidious is that they're all <i>too</i> human \u2014 in the worst possible way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T08:36:30-08:00","id":1430572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1429970#post1429970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. If the Lysenko\u2019s methods worked the Technocracy would have won already. Unfortunately for them, human reaction and belief is difficult to predict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - Convention Book: Progenitors even talks about how during the Industrial Revolution they planned to simultaneously launch a series of technologies that would deal with the pollution brought about by industrialisation ... but the Sleepers just refused to buy into it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T10:13:01-08:00","id":1430586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430572#post1430572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes - Convention Book: Progenitors even talks about how during the Industrial Revolution they planned to simultaneously launch a series of technologies that would deal with the pollution brought about by industrialisation ... but the Sleepers just refused to buy into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it in revised?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T14:52:00-08:00","id":1430614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430586#post1430586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it in revised?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T15:03:06-08:00","id":1430615,"title":"","content":"Not doubting you; but could you provide a page reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T16:37:57-08:00","id":1430628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430615#post1430615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not doubting you; but could you provide a page reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>P. 41, the sidebar about the micro-methodologies, &quot;Preservationists&quot; writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T18:03:45-08:00","id":1430632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430628#post1430628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P. 41, the sidebar about the micro-methodologies, &quot;Preservationists&quot; writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I have ADHD, so it's a struggle for me to read through these long books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T15:05:09-08:00","id":1431329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1430531#post1430531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'll note, in your defense, that you're not the only one who would prefer the Nephandi to have some sort of redeeming element buried somewhere in their philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No 'redeeming element'. That necessarily involves an external judgment imposed upon their system of beliefs. The Nephandi have to be as right as anyone else, if we're going to take seriously what Mage claims to be about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26588-melendwyr","name":"Melendwyr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T12:14:08-08:00","id":1431414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melendwyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1431329#post1431329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No 'redeeming element'. That necessarily involves an external judgment imposed upon their system of beliefs. The Nephandi have to be as right as anyone else, if we're going to take seriously what Mage claims to be about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well hold on, there is no promise that everyone is equally right. Yes in Mage metaphysics belief reshapes reality but surprisingly there isn't any evidence (either for or against) that belief reshapes morality. Indeed, how would anyone even be able to tell? So it's not so much that all the factions are equally right, it's more that all the factions are convinced that they are right but don't actually know. In that regards the Nephandi are very much certain of their views (we think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T12:55:36-08:00","id":1431612,"title":"","content":"If, as the game suggests, reality is truly subjective in the Mage universe, the only constraint on anything is the collective opinion of the totality of avatars. That's the only objective truth. Everything else is a construct - or, depending on how we look at it, a lie or a made-truth.<br /> <br /> Moral standards are no more real and objective than physical laws - most of which are mutable by mages on Earth, practically all of which seem to be mutable by mages in the spirit worlds. It may not be the case that mages can truly alter logic, but they certainly seem to able to determine which axioms apply to observable phenomena.<br /> <br /> WW was never very good at using themes that arose from mechanics or basic setting principles - it always tried to impose them on the system arbitrarily. As opposed to the works of individual authors - Jenna Moran (formerly R. Borgstrom), who has a background in math and is a brilliant designer who makes games that naturally produce certain kinds of behavior in the players. WW's moral themes were always tacked on, and never was that more the case than with Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26588-melendwyr","name":"Melendwyr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T13:41:35-08:00","id":1431620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melendwyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1431612#post1431612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, as the game suggests, reality is truly subjective in the Mage universe, the only constraint on anything is the collective opinion of the totality of avatars. That's the only objective truth. Everything else is a construct - or, depending on how we look at it, a lie or a made-truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wish to play it that way, go for it! But even Mage as written isn't that simplistic. MRev described Cosmological Constants and Historical Inertia; M20 has Earthly Foundations. As a result of these, you can't even say that \u201creality is truly subjective\u201d is an objective truth of the setting. At the <i>very least</i>, there are some things that are remarkably resistant to being shaped even by the Consensus. There are things that exist <i>independent of</i> the Consensus, and there are things that exist <i>despite</i> the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T15:39:16-08:00","id":1431625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melendwyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1431612#post1431612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, as the game suggests, reality is truly subjective in the Mage universe, the only constraint on anything is the collective opinion of the totality of avatars. That's the only objective truth. Everything else is a construct</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll leave you a philosophical conundrum<br /> <br /> If the only constraint on anything it's the collective opinion of the totality of avatars.<br /> <br /> And then the collective of Avatars decide Nephandi goals are evil.<br /> <br /> How would this be different from the Word of God (aka, objective truth) saying they're evil?<br /> <br /> As I see it, only an opinion outside this opinion could judge them as &quot;not evil&quot; (btw, admiting that it's tanamount to admit the Consensus doesn't create truth, as there can be other truths outside of it) - and even then, this opinion would be delusional unless it can change the Avatar collective's opinion<br /> <br /> Note that, as others and myself have said, Mage never goes so far. There are many canon ways of interpreting the reach of the Consensus as less than absolute - but it's entertaining to think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-09-2021, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T09:31:02-08:00","id":1431840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melendwyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1431612#post1431612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, as the game suggests, reality is truly subjective in the Mage universe, the only constraint on anything is the collective opinion of the totality of avatars. That's the only objective truth. Everything else is a construct - or, depending on how we look at it, a lie or a made-truth.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that at first glance Mage does present all of reality as subjective and that you <i>can</i> play the game that way, that doesn't have to be the case and indeed the general indication is it isn't.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> says, there are things (cosmological constants) that are either beyond the reach of the Consensus or so deeply embedded as to seem beyond reach. I will freely admit that I prefer to use CCs as little as possible, but the very fact that they are in the game indicates that reality is more complicated than pure subjectivity.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, no one acts like they are wrong but can make themselves right if they convince enough people. The Traditions and the Technocracy both think they are doing the right things. They understand that they still have to convince society at large, of course, but they are not waiting until that time to call their actions moral. Nor are they magically changing morality in their area or using horizon realms to create small pockets where they are right*. They either think of morality as a social construct or as an objective yardstick to be appealed to, neither of which is a metaphysical morality controlled by the consensus.<br /> <br /> *They may magically enforce consequences for certain behaviors, but that's different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T07:46:35-08:00","id":1432912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427196#post1427196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is ultimately true; but it's possible for the Awakened to mitigate this. The more Sleepers can do on their own, the less the Awakened have to do for them; and the more democratic and in charge of their own fate the Sleepers can be.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Technocracy counters that argument by pointing to just how stupid the Sleepers have been with the gifts already afforded them. They do not trust the Sleepers (with good reason, they argue), and because of this they seek to subvert democratic systems so that they can overrule the Sleepers whenever they think they're being stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious downside of that viewpoint is that absolute power corrupts absolutely; when given to a group of Enlightened Scientists who can control reality with their smartphones and spaceships...<br /> <br /> The absence of democracy almost always creates disaster (benevolent dictators are very much the exception, not the rule). I'm sure the Lions of Zion and Chevra Kadisha could tell you that... you know, after Germany. Hong Kong would tell you; so would the Uyghurs, if the Technocracy would let them out. That's right, I'm blaming the Technocracy for the Second Holocaust. You know why? The Syndicate controls the money and the NWO control governments and information. If the Five Metal Dragons (Chinese Technocracy) wanted to, they could easily stop the Second Holocaust.<br /> <br /> So, why does the Technocracy keep subverting democratic systems despite the fact that it's gone disastrously in history (tyrannical systems (some of which were supported by the Technocracy) created the 20th Century, which, while carrying great progress in the free world, was the bloodiest century in human history outside of the free world)? I'm not suggesting that the other factions are blameless on this front; the Order of Hermes and Wu Lung clearly wand to re-install their feudalistic systems, while the Knights Templar clearly want to install a theocracy. However, the Virtual Adepts, Euthanatoi, Lions of Zion, and Chevra Kadisha could very clearly see that the Axis Powers were <i>E</i><i>vil</i>; why couldn't the Technocracy? And why couldn't the Council? Moreover, why did the Technocracy kill Turing three years after the start of the Allied Pogrom, which purged mages, most likely Nephandi, still loyal to the Axis Powers? Was it really because of his experiments in the Digital Web, or was it a HYDRA v. Howard Stark situation? <br /> <br /> Before you call this a conspiracy theory, the World of Darkness (<i>especially</i> Mage) is <i>all</i> conspiracy fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or they could have come up with a more humane way to acquire the special ingredients. (By the way: are you aware that solar panels require rare earth elements as well? Solar power looks like a good option until you look into just what is needed to make them.)<br /> <br /> One reason behind my Earthly foundations argument is to come up with a reason why an Enlightened Scientist might have chosen to go with arbitrary choices like requiring rare earth elements, why the Void Engineers formatting of space into Conventional Space results in a vacuum, and so on. In short, the decision to do things the way they did was more involved than just arbitrary, capricious, pointless choices. \u201cThis is what you have to do in order to maintain full compatibility with the Earthly Foundations\u201d becomes the reason why the Enlightened Scientists went with the technology that they did. </div> </div> </div>I was about to mention this! I'm personally interested in quantum dot solar cells and mirror-based solar power (I'm an engineering student and a bit of a photonics geek). Of course, when you're in a world of magickal Traditions who now have greater acceptance of hypertech and weird science...<br /> I talked a bit about how Trad labs might be competing with Technocracy labs on COVID-19 cures. They also might be competing with Technocracy labs on solar panels and other energy tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T08:11:26-08:00","id":1432913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1427510#post1427510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Capitalism plays a huge role in this, and it's weird that anyone could think otherwise. We produce more food than anyone could eat, and so much of it gets thrown away. We have an overproduction problem and you would see it if you bother to debate with any informed socialist.<br /> <br /> Capitalism plays a significant role in where commodities are distributed. Which is to say, they're distributed where there's money, and often produced where it's cheapest to produce. Which is to say corporations gravitate to places where they can pay workers pennies on the dollar while collective massive amounts of money on the results of their labor. Since these places are poor it's not very profitable to distribute commodities there - instead they get distributed where people will pay for them. And even then, overproduction means that a significant amount of these commodities don't get sold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overproduction and scarcity, while related, are not opposites. Scarcity is just the limited availability of resources, which is guaranteed by the Laws of Thermodynamics. Even if you overproduce food, unless you use magick, food will still be scarce because there will ultimately always be a finite supply of food.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Libertarians are hampered by committing themselves to a flawed ideology that won't work out the way they think it will. One needs only look at Paul Ryan's record as Speaker of the House to see how applied libertarianism actually further restricts the distribution of resources, and mostly restricts it from the poorest people.<br /> <br /> An &quot;intelligent libertarian&quot; is in it to get rich, not to improve society. The most intelligent libertarian understands that only a few people have any chance of acquiring serious wealth. Anything they say will be geared toward their own self interest, and can thus be discarded as heavily biased. A truly intelligent libertarian would see the ideology as the cannibalistic con job that it is and get out.<br /> <br /> Barely restrained capitalism is destroying the environment and killing people. There's no valid defense for it.<br /> </div> </div> </div>That is very clearly an oversimplification of libertarianism. Also, Paul Ryan? His support for tax breaks for petroleum industry (tax structures which favor one industry over another, which most American libertarians don't support, with a minority of them supporting tax structures which disadvantage industries responsible for negative externalities) and a ban on same-sex marriage (the usage of force to restrict the rights of the individual) show that he is not a libertarian as defined by most left-libertarians, center-libertarians, or right-libertarians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T09:33:51-08:00","id":1432919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1432913#post1432913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overproduction and scarcity, while related, are not opposites. Scarcity is just the limited availability of resources, which is guaranteed by the Laws of Thermodynamics. Even if you overproduce food, unless you use magick, food will still be scarce because there will ultimately always be a finite supply of food.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bogus argument.<br /> <br /> No system, no matter how utopical, ever wanted or pretended to have infinite food - that would effectively destroy the world and beyond with it's impossible mass.<br /> <br /> You don't need to do that to solve scarcity because the basic needs of humans are finite and very well established, even if our greed knows no bounds.<br /> <br /> The whole arguent about scarcity being &quot;unsolvable&quot; because &quot;human desire it's infinite&quot; it's horseshit: <i>We're living in a world where the most basic Maslow Needs aren't being fulfilled</i> - <b><i>that's Scarcity</i></b>. Not that you're unable to build an empire in Pluto, or whatever stupid thing boored rich people desire. To philosophically think that because you can always desire more, there will never be enough for everyone it's an argument whose makers trully deserve the title of &quot;<i>decadent bourgeois</i>&quot;.<br /> You need to be very much at the top of the pyramid to have reached the point where <i>Thermodinamics themselves</i> are what limits your so-called &quot;needs&quot;. More so, you have to be willing to *take more* resources to fulfill those desires, even while you see that the rest of the people can't even fulfill the most basic needs. That such people lament &quot;scarcity&quot; it's a bad joke<br /> <br /> At the moment humans produce enough food to feed all the very much *finite* amount of humans that exist at a certain period of time, it's at least <i>suspicious </i>(as in, one could suspect &quot;the system&quot; has some flaw) to <i>fail </i>at feeding all humans in that period. Now, feeding all humans depends on more than just having enough food for everyone (which we *have*), as you have to distribute it - that's where &quot;the system&quot; come in. Economics it's the science of allocating resources.<br /> <br /> Under Capitalism resources are allocated where they would produce more proffit. Hence poor people die of malnourishment, no money no food. There are economical justifications for this cruelty, but Thermodynamics ain't what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Feeding all of humanity it's not a <i>physical </i>imposibility, it's not <i>beyond science</i>. It may be economically infeasible at our current state of development, <i>at most</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is very clearly an oversimplification of libertarianism. </div> </div> </div>Trully it is. But then, do we <i>really </i>want to debate such a topic in a thread about the Technocracy &amp; magical unicorns?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> So, why does the Technocracy keep subverting democratic systems despite the fact that it's gone disastrously in history (tyrannical systems (some of which were supported by the Technocracy) created the 20th Century, which, while carrying great progress in the free world, was the bloodiest century in human history outside of the free world)? I'm not suggesting that the other factions are blameless on this front; the Order of Hermes and Wu Lung clearly wand to re-install their feudalistic systems, while the Knights Templar clearly want to install a theocracy. However, the Virtual Adepts, Euthanatoi, Lions of Zion, and Chevra Kadisha could very clearly see that the Axis Powers were <i>E</i><i>vil</i>; why couldn't the Technocracy? And why couldn't the Council? Moreover, why did the Technocracy kill Turing three years after the start of the Allied Pogrom, which purged mages, most likely Nephandi, still loyal to the Axis Powers? Was it really because of his experiments in the Digital Web, or was it a HYDRA v. Howard Stark situation? </div> </div> </div>Etherites also saw that Axis powers were evil, and there's even many canon Etherite characters that *actually* fougth against the Axis in the books. But I guess you don't like Etherites because they were/are in favor of the Comunist experiment :P Interestingly, many would tell you that the experiment failed because of the Union...<br /> <br /> <i>If we enter in conspiracy theories</i>,<i> there's theories for all tastes</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, I would say Technocracy aren't the good guys (neither are the Traditions) And to understand why, you have to look to more than mortal affairs. The Technocracy has an agenda that can be cruel and downrigth criminal but, they believe, will end in an improvement of the cuality of life of all of humanity.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy may well have been on board with Mao, because he had an ideology that was very hard on mystical practices of the Wu Lung, allowing to take them off with far more ease. But then, Wul Lung were in favor of the Yellow Emperor.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Axis, Technocracy eventually went against them (when it was discovered they were full of Nephandi). Prior to that...well, the Technocracy never cared a whole lot about the loss of innocent human life &quot;for the greater good&quot;. So swit yourself: Since you like Libertarians, you could say that the Technocracy saw the regime as a potential tool against Comunism and it's evil Etherites. See, there's a conspiracy theory for you.<br /> <br /> And Technocracy has likely been behind the current definition of Democracy too. Defeating divinely appointed Monarchs makes sense for their agenda, and the surge of democracy (and liberalism) as understood in modern ideology it's paralel to the &quot;enlightenment&quot; era, that's so cherished by the Union.<br /> <br /> If one catter to the conspiracy theories that show the Technocracy as evil, but never to those that show it as doing good...obviously they would end looking as pure evil.<br /> <br /> You could also chalk some of this as the consequence of the Technocracy not being a monolith, not really. Any organization that has grown too much has masters with conflicting agendas. Also corruption and whatnot.<br /> There are a lot of &quot;spices&quot; to make your own take on the Technocratical stance. As an organization they're hardly &quot;the unsung heros of humanity&quot; unless you buy all of their propaganda, but they don't need to be pure evil either unless you make them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-21-2021, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T15:55:42-08:00","id":1432973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1432919#post1432919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Etherites also saw that Axis powers were evil, and there's even many canon Etherite characters that *actually* fougth against the Axis in the books. But I guess you don't like Etherites because they were/are in favor of the Comunist experiment :P Interestingly, many would tell you that the experiment failed because of the Union...</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I was under the impression that some Etherites joined with the Axis Powers because Hitler was very tolerant of BS science and not very tolerant of actual science (he reprimanded one of his top scientists IRL for teaching quantum physics because it was supposedly &quot;Jewish science&quot;; can't imagine what he would have thought of Relativity).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Technocracy has likely been behind the current definition of Democracy too. Defeating divinely appointed Monarchs makes sense for their agenda, and the surge of democracy (and liberalism) as understood in modern ideology it's paralel to the &quot;enlightenment&quot; era, that's so cherished by the Union. </div> </div> </div>Was that an achievement of the Order of Reason, the group who distributed magick to the people in the name of God and all mankind, or the Technocratic Union, the group who frequently lies to and kills humanity in the name of their invisible masters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T19:26:36-08:00","id":1432997,"title":"","content":"On a side tangent has any mage on either side considered the Transcendental Argument for the Non-existence of God (TANG) &amp; how that would apply to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T04:51:00-08:00","id":1433039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1432973#post1432973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason I was under the impression that some Etherites joined with the Axis Powers because Hitler was very tolerant of BS science and not very tolerant of actual science (he reprimanded one of his top scientists IRL for teaching quantum physics because it was supposedly &quot;Jewish science&quot;; can't imagine what he would have thought of Relativity).</div> </div> </div> </div>Etherites are not purveyors of BS science because, as they would argue, all science is BS until it turns out to be right. They would enjoy more freedom of opportunity to investigate theories outside the norm, but Hitler's opinion on 'jewish science' would have alienated many SoEs because they don't like being told what they can and can't research. To be fair, it would have attracted others who were still fuming about the whole Ether debacle.<br /> <br /> I would still place many Etherites on the Axis side, but for a different reason. The Etherites are, in my mind anyway, highly associated with the ideals and motifs of golden age and pre golden age science fiction. That includes a healthy dose of iconoclasty and fighting against evil, but it also includes an unhealthy dose of 'benevolent' fascism, colonialism, and racism. The system of government of the fascist powers would have appealed to many Etherites even if the motives of those at the top did not. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1432973#post1432973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that an achievement of the Order of Reason, the group who distributed magick to the people in the name of God and all mankind, or the Technocratic Union, the group who frequently lies to and kills humanity in the name of their invisible masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a secret conspiracy, the Technocracy are well placed to work well behind almost any government, be it democratic, communist, fascist, etc. As I recall, they've experimented around with many forms of government to see what fits their needs and the reason they were on both sides of WWII is that there was quite a bit of internal dispute over which ones did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T14:11:18-08:00","id":1433097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1432997#post1432997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side tangent has any mage on either side considered the Transcendental Argument for the Non-existence of God (TANG) &amp; how that would apply to them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the TAG, or some primitive variant of it, was the basis of the Gabrielite-remnant faction that accepted that they weren't channeling God's power; it stands to reason that, the NWO, essentially faithless versions of the Gabrielites, may have considered the TANG in order to get away from their Christian history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T15:20:23-08:00","id":1433108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433097#post1433097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, the TAG, or some primitive variant of it, was the basis of the Gabrielite-remnant faction that accepted that they weren't channeling God's power; it stands to reason that, the NWO, essentially faithless versions of the Gabrielites, may have considered the TANG in order to get away from their Christian history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly do all factions not realize that their worldviews require presuppositions? Even the Technocrats don't realize they are bending the laws of physics in ways that suspend different laws at different times. I mean yeah they can pretend they don't but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T15:39:05-08:00","id":1433111,"title":"","content":"Actually, per the upcoming <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, the Technocracy is very much aware that they're bending the laws of physics as Sleepers understand them. They just don't buy into the idea that what they do is fundamentally the same as what the Superstitionists do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T14:28:03-08:00","id":1433181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1432973#post1432973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that an achievement of the Order of Reason, the group who distributed magick to the people in the name of God and all mankind, or the Technocratic Union, the group who frequently lies to and kills humanity in the name of their invisible masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>As per <i>Ramnesis</i><br /> <br /> Just add that you can't really sepparate the two in such a strict fashion.<br /> <br /> OoR helped a lot of evils in the name of the greater good, too, they participated in witch hunts and paved or directly orchestrated the colonization of the &quot;new world&quot;. The Union doubled down on that, but everything that's wrong with them was present in the Order. People can do both good and evil, and also be wrong about which it's which. An organization can, and most likely will, have people that are corrupt and people that trully believe in the party line.<br /> <br /> OoR wasn't transformed into the Union by an act of Satan (well, maybe a little bit - Nephandi and whatnot), one can't ignore that since it's inception it had powerful internal conflicts. That ended causing the great reorganization. In the same vein, they didn't just *stop* caring about thier lofty ideals at that point - it's simply that the forces of corruption became more prevalent and the ideals were forced into a second plane.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T18:15:39-08:00","id":1433442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433111#post1433111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, per the upcoming <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, the Technocracy is very much aware that they're bending the laws of physics as Sleepers understand them. They just don't buy into the idea that what they do is fundamentally the same as what the Superstitionists do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What, because they can use science to explain away how they fundamentally abuse science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T19:38:52-08:00","id":1433454,"title":"","content":"That would be the Traditions' argument, yes. Obviously, it's not the argument that the Technocracy would lay out. <i>Their</i> argument hinges on the technomancer/mystic divide, which is key because the reason for the divide is that one side views Magick as an exercise of Enlightened Will while the other side views Science as an exercise of Enlightened technique. Mystics put intent (what you're trying to do) front and center; technomancers put method (how you're doing it) front and center. <br /> <br /> On the one hand, this distinction means that technomancers don't get to discard their Instruments or to Work Without Focus; on the other hand, it's entirely possible that this technomantic mindset is necessary for learning and using the Technocratic Spheres (which aren't <i>better</i> than their traditional counterparts, but are different in useful ways such as Primal Utility being better at making Wonders than Prime is, and providing access to Primal Ventures). <br /> <br /> The closest thing the Technocrats come to abusing science is in their decision to stick to building on the Earthly Foundations (or phrased another way, being reductionist). From their perspective, the Etherites aren't true Scientists precisely because they reject reductionism: <i>their</i> theories are built on shifting sand, and thus are more susceptible to paradoxes, something that a sufficiently refined Technocratic innovation doesn't have to worry about. <br /> <br /> By contrast: to the Etherites, the Technocrats are abusing science because their insistence on conformity to a single universal Focus blinds them to alternatives. <br /> <br /> That, and Etherites tend to be much more comfortable with the Avatar than Technocrats are with Genius: it's entirely possible that one of the purposes of Conditioning is to harness (Etherites would say \u201cmuzzle\u201d) the Genius, making it easier for the Technocrat to direct her Scientific efforts as she sees fit instead of having spontaneous sparks of inspiration mucking everything up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T08:17:01-08:00","id":1433706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433454#post1433454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the Traditions' argument, yes. Obviously, it's not the argument that the Technocracy would lay out. <i>Their</i> argument hinges on the technomancer/mystic divide, which is key because the reason for the divide is that one side views Magick as an exercise of Enlightened Will while the other side views Science as an exercise of Enlightened technique. Mystics put intent (what you're trying to do) front and center; technomancers put method (how you're doing it) front and center.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;abusing science,&quot; I didn't mean &quot;twisting the scientific method to their own ends&quot; (which the Technocracy does do), I meant &quot;muting what they want to be immutable laws of physics, thereby defeating the entire point.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the method over intent... that holds up when dealing with witches, chaos magicians, and shamans, but what about high ritual magi, the people that the Order of Reason broke off from? They use numerology, sacred mathematics, astrology, and whatever else... to determine when they even <i>perform a ritual</i>! Then ritual purifications, prayers, excorcisms and awakening spirits of various materials and weapons, warding... to a Hermetic, the methodology is just as important as the intent. In contrast, to a Reality Hacker (widely considered technomancers), the result is more important than the methodology. Whether a Reality Hacker creates a virus that wrecks computer systems (Correspondence 3/Entropy 3) or uses that Cyberpunk rote to pull a stick of dynamite out of virtual space (Correspondence 2/Matter 2, from the Virtual Adept book, I think Revised) and blow up the computers, the method doesn't really matter. What matters is the change brought about by destroying the computers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the one hand, this distinction means that technomancers don't get to discard their Instruments or to Work Without Focus; on the other hand, it's entirely possible that this technomantic mindset is necessary for learning and using the Technocratic Spheres (which aren't <i>better</i> than their traditional counterparts, but are different in useful ways such as Primal Utility being better at making Wonders than Prime is, and providing access to Primal Ventures).<br /> <br /> The closest thing the Technocrats come to abusing science is in their decision to stick to building on the Earthly Foundations (or phrased another way, being reductionist). </div> </div> </div>Again, by &quot;abusing science,&quot; I meant &quot;muting what they want to be immutable laws of physics, thereby defeating the entire point.&quot; Think about it: if you say that something is an immutable law, for example, no FTL travel, then something like teleporting humans (impossible, even with quantum mechanics), <i>something that mutes an immutable law</i>, makes those laws entirely worthless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From their perspective, the Etherites aren't true Scientists precisely because they reject reductionism: <i>their</i> theories are built on shifting sand, and thus are more susceptible to paradoxes, something that a sufficiently refined Technocratic innovation doesn't have to worry about.<br /> <br /> By contrast: to the Etherites, the Technocrats are abusing science because their insistence on conformity to a single universal Focus blinds them to alternatives.<br /> <br /> That, and Etherites tend to be much more comfortable with the Avatar than Technocrats are with Genius: it's entirely possible that one of the purposes of Conditioning is to harness (Etherites would say \u201cmuzzle\u201d) the Genius, making it easier for the Technocrat to direct her Scientific efforts as she sees fit instead of having spontaneous sparks of inspiration mucking everything up. </div> </div> </div>It's funny that you say that, because from an IRL perspective, the Technocracy aren't real scientists. Now, you might wonder why I say this. The answer? Well...<br /> <br /> The Technocracy uses DimSci as a replacement for Spirit. They have observed that the &quot;Superstitionists&quot; can summon, awaken, and bind spirits. The Technocracy cannot. Yet, they do not seem to have formed and tested a hypothesis about why they can't. They seem to be content to not push the bounds of science. We, as observers, know that DimSci can't do all that stuff because it is formulated to work with the dimensions, not the entities there-in. But you'd think if the Void Engineers were real scientists, they'd be trying to master &quot;xenobiology.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could list things all day about phenomena that the Technocracy can observe, but not hypothesize about or test because of their limited paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","user":"JagneStormskull","date":". 01-28-2021, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T08:45:34-08:00","id":1433711,"title":"","content":"What laws of physics? <br /> <br /> I know there are stuff that *can't* be changed. The Earthly Foundations. And yet, the laws of reality are mutable, and can shift, according to Reality Zones, areas (Constructs! Outer Space!) and everything else. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy does not view anything like that. Or more accurately, they believe that what they do is not only according to the laws of reality as they discover it, but also are safer due to the fact that they're closer to the 'truth', as can be seen in reduced Paradox. And when they enter a Reality Zone or a place Consensus is warped and their fancy toys fail? Well, that's obviously due to a technologically-hostile dimension and Reality Deviance interference, causing their machines to break down and need Primium backups and countermeasures. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocracy uses DimSci as a replacement for Spirit. They have observed that the &quot;Superstitionists&quot; can summon, awaken, and bind spirits. The Technocracy cannot. Yet, they do not seem to have formed and tested a hypothesis about why they can't. They seem to be content to not push the bounds of science. We, as observers, know that DimSci can't do all that stuff because it is formulated to work with the dimensions, not the entities there-in. But you'd think if the Void Engineers were real scientists, they'd be trying to master &quot;xenobiology.&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;Various tests by esteemed scientists have noted that Extra-dimensional entities are not only mostly hostile to human life, but attempts to coerce them into working with you have a tendency to backfire. Either because forcible conversion has a chance of failure and increases hostility, but because the various tasks required by the Entities are often neutral at best to harmful to the Technocracy's timetable.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Holy shit dude, where have you been? Out here, everything is trying to kill us. Even the EDEs. No point in trying to negotiate with them, because they either backstab you or it's not worth it. I remember someone doing that before. Gabe, I think. Last I heard, he got melted into a puddle of goop in his armour by the EDE he was trying to court. So yeah, don't do it.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Attempts to bargain with Extra-Dimensional Entities is a violation of the Precepts of Damian, Article Three, who demands the creation of the Gauntlet and persecution of those who breach the dimensional barriers. Attempts to bargain with EDEs have a noted failure rate, and are a noted practice of Reality Deviants, who would sell people to Nephandic and the like. Any who attempt to bind and bribe EDEs are to be investigated and sent to room 101.&quot; <br /> <br /> Mage science is literally politics and personal worldview. In fact, the entirety of the world is composed out of politics and worldview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T04:26:39-08:00","id":1433787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433706#post1433706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the method over intent... that holds up when dealing with witches, chaos magicians, and shamans, but what about high ritual magi, the people that the Order of Reason broke off from? They use numerology, sacred mathematics, astrology, and whatever else... to determine when they even <i>perform a ritual</i>! Then ritual purifications, prayers, excorcisms and awakening spirits of various materials and weapons, warding... to a Hermetic, the methodology is just as important as the intent. In contrast, to a Reality Hacker (widely considered technomancers), the result is more important than the methodology. Whether a Reality Hacker creates a virus that wrecks computer systems (Correspondence 3/Entropy 3) or uses that Cyberpunk rote to pull a stick of dynamite out of virtual space (Correspondence 2/Matter 2, from the Virtual Adept book, I think Revised) and blow up the computers, the method doesn't really matter. What matters is the change brought about by destroying the computers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention that. In my games, I tend to run the mystic/technomancer divide in the Traditions on a much more individualistic basis; and I tend to put a lot of Hermetics on the technomancer side despite not using technological Instruments, while there are many VAs who are full-on mystics despite having distinctly technological Instruments. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433706#post1433706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, by \u201cabusing science,\u201d I meant \u201cmuting what they want to be immutable laws of physics, thereby defeating the entire point.\u201d Think about it: if you say that something is an immutable law, for example, no FTL travel, then something like teleporting humans (impossible, even with quantum mechanics), <i>something that mutes an immutable law</i>, makes those laws entirely worthless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two points here: first, \u201cimmutable laws\u201d is an ideal that the Technocracy works toward, not an already-achieved reality. The various Conventions vary on how much importance they place in this ideal (the Syndicate is really big on it, which is why Syndics tend to favor Coincidental Effects when they need to alter reality at all; while the Void Engineers go wild with their Hypertechnology), but they all agree that they'd prefer not to have to change anything. <br /> <br /> Second, Technocrats tend to prefer to \u201cadd to\u201d or reinforce natural laws rather than to alter them. To them, there's a most natural way to do things, and a Technocratic Reality Zone is what you get when you reinforce and build upon the natural laws of reality: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new Roman\">Throughout the world in this 21<sup>st</sup> century, the Technocratic vision of reality hold the coincidental edge, not simply because of the Union's indoctrination \u2026 but because science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.</span><br /> \u2014M20 p.613</div>Note that this <i>isn't</i> presented from the Technocracy's point of view; it's stated as a basic truth. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433706#post1433706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny that you say that, because from an IRL perspective, the Technocracy aren't real scientists. Now, you might wonder why I say this. The answer? Well...<br /> <br /> The Technocracy uses DimSci as a replacement for Spirit. They have observed that the \u201cSuperstitionists\u201d can summon, awaken, and bind spirits. The Technocracy cannot. Yet, they do not seem to have formed and tested a hypothesis about why they can't. They seem to be content to not push the bounds of science. We, as observers, know that DimSci can't do all that stuff because it is formulated to work with the dimensions, not the entities there-in. But you'd think if the Void Engineers were real scientists, they'd be trying to master \u201cxenobiology.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Dimensional Science <i>can</i> summon, bind, and ward against EDEs. It just doesn't <i>explicitly</i> grant the ability to enslave EDEs \u2014 which isn't to say that Dimensional Scientists <i>can't</i> do that: the Technocratic Sphere write-ups are no more all-inclusive in their coverage of <i>everything</i> that a Sphere can do than their more traditional counterparts are; and just because the write-up doesn't explicitly say that you <i>can</i> do something doesn't automatically mean that you <i>can't</i>. Rather, the Sphere write-up covers the primary uses of the Sphere, which in the case of Dimensional Science mostly deals with Gauntlet manipulation and defense against or destruction of hostile EDEs: more Ghostbusting than seances. <br /> <br /> But as Accelerator points out, such fields of research tend to be frowned on by the bulk of the Technocracy, as it <i>does</i> have an agenda and thus priorities on research. It's not that different from how certain lines of research are banned IRL because of questionable ethics, or de facto banned because everyone agrees that it's \u201cjunk science\u201d. <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that they're disregarded <i>entirely</i>; it's just that the departments that engage in such research have a rather seedy reputation. For instance, there's the Syndicate's Special Projects Division (which in my games is more <i>Fringe</i> than Pentex, and includes funding for the likes of Orpheus, but is still something of a \u201cdirty secret\u201d of the Syndicate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-29-2021, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T11:30:57-08:00","id":1433811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433787#post1433787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny you should mention that. In my games, I tend to run the mystic/technomancer divide in the Traditions on a much more individualistic basis; and I tend to put a lot of Hermetics on the technomancer side despite not using technological Instruments, while there are many VAs who are full-on mystics despite having distinctly technological Instruments.<br /> <br /> <br /> Two points here: first, \u201cimmutable laws\u201d is an ideal that the Technocracy works toward, not an already-achieved reality. The various Conventions vary on how much importance they place in this ideal (the Syndicate is really big on it, which is why Syndics tend to favor Coincidental Effects when they need to alter reality at all; while the Void Engineers go wild with their Hypertechnology), but they all agree that they'd prefer not to have to change anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said &quot;want,&quot; not &quot;are.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dimensional Science <i>can</i> summon, bind, and ward against EDEs. It just doesn't <i>explicitly</i> grant the ability to enslave EDEs \u2014 which isn't to say that Dimensional Scientists <i>can't</i> do that: the Technocratic Sphere write-ups are no more all-inclusive in their coverage of <i>everything</i> that a Sphere can do than their more traditional counterparts are; and just because the write-up doesn't explicitly say that you <i>can</i> do something doesn't automatically mean that you <i>can't</i>. Rather, the Sphere write-up covers the primary uses of the Sphere, which in the case of Dimensional Science mostly deals with Gauntlet manipulation and defense against or destruction of hostile EDEs: more Ghostbusting than seances.<br /> <br /> But as Accelerator points out, such fields of research tend to be frowned on by the bulk of the Technocracy, as it <i>does</i> have an agenda and thus priorities on research. It's not that different from how certain lines of research are banned IRL because of questionable ethics, or de facto banned because everyone agrees that it's \u201cjunk science\u201d. </div> </div> </div>The difference between &quot;junk science&quot; IRL and &quot;junk science&quot; in Mage are that the former is &quot;a phenomenon is impossible, so stop talking about it like it is&quot; while the latter is &quot;a phenomenon has been observed, but it's a tool of our enemies, so we don't want to research it.&quot; As for the ethics, warding against EDEs would certainly be a useful defense technique for Void Engineers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is not to say that they're disregarded <i>entirely</i>; it's just that the departments that engage in such research have a rather seedy reputation. For instance, there's the Syndicate's Special Projects Division (which in my games is more <i>Fringe</i> than Pentex, and includes funding for the likes of Orpheus, but is still something of a \u201cdirty secret\u201d of the Syndicate). </div> </div> </div>Now, this is a Rule Zero situation, but wasn't Special Projects Division eaten by werewol... I mean killed off mysteriously after the Avatar Storm? Just curious, was it repaired in your game, or did it just never disappear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T11:32:18-08:00","id":1433812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433711#post1433711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Attempts to bargain with Extra-Dimensional Entities is a violation of the Precepts of Damian, Article Three, who demands the creation of the Gauntlet and persecution of those who breach the dimensional barriers. Attempts to bargain with EDEs have a noted failure rate, and are a noted practice of Reality Deviants, who would sell people to Nephandic and the like. Any who attempt to bind and bribe EDEs are to be investigated and sent to room 101.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Anyone who puts the Precepts of Damian before SCIENCE! should report to the Chaoticians for immediate deprogramming.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T17:06:23-08:00","id":1433856,"title":"","content":"The only reason why the Technocracy is successful as it is because they're a Weaver cult, just like how Pentex is wildly successful by aide and allegiance to the Wyrm. The only different between Pentex and the Technocracy is that Pentex is fully cognizant of being vassals to the Wyrm; while the Technocracy is unaware of the Weaver because the Weaver works subtly and through the low-whirring shifts of the OneSong. <br /> <br /> Also Earthly Foundations are BS in Mage because any Mage that is Arete 7+ or above can completely wreck any notion of Earthly Foundations. The only reason why they don't do it is because with their high insight they already know the trivialities of the Ascension War and Earth itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T18:09:39-08:00","id":1433861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433812#post1433812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Anyone who puts the Precepts of Damian before SCIENCE! should report to the Chaoticians for immediate deprogramming.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The heck are the chaoticians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T18:13:09-08:00","id":1433862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433811#post1433811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference between &quot;junk science&quot; IRL and &quot;junk science&quot; in Mage are that the former is &quot;a phenomenon is impossible, so stop talking about it like it is&quot; while the latter is &quot;a phenomenon has been observed, but it's a tool of our enemies, so we don't want to research it.&quot; As for the ethics, warding against EDEs would certainly be a useful defense technique for Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like the wards placed upon pretty much every construct against scrying and EDE attacks? Those?<br /> <br /> No offense, but why *wouldn't* Void Engineers have any of them? They literally go into the Umbra. They just put it down as 'anti-psychic field against aliens' or 'phase-space disruptor to prevent EDE infiltration'.<br /> <br /> edit: And another thing. Most Junk science is basically thrown away due to politics, Time Table, or just plain inconsistency with their own paradigm. They *do* study Junk science. It's just through their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 01-29-2021, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T18:30:57-08:00","id":1433863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433811#post1433811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between &quot;junk science&quot; IRL and &quot;junk science&quot; in Mage are that the former is &quot;a phenomenon is impossible, so stop talking about it like it is&quot; while the latter is &quot;a phenomenon has been observed, but it's a tool of our enemies, so we don't want to research it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Technocracy chose not to research things simply because the Traditions use it, they wouldn't research <i>anything</i>. Try again: what criteria does the Union use to decide what direction to take their research? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433811#post1433811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the ethics, warding against EDEs would certainly be a useful defense technique for Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would be, and is. Reread Dimensional Science: it includes the ability to ward against EDEs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433811#post1433811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this is a Rule Zero situation, but wasn't Special Projects Division eaten by werewol... I mean killed off mysteriously after the Avatar Storm? Just curious, was it repaired in your game, or did it just never disappear?</div> </div> </div> </div> In my Chronicles, SPD is more than just Pentex-related stuff; and in fact, the part of it that was Pentex-related was actually a <i>small</i> part of it. And yes, that part of it mysteriously disappeared. But the rest of SPD \u2014 the bulk of it that had nothing to do with Pentex \u2014 never disappeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-31-2021, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T18:56:35-08:00","id":1433865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433856#post1433856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason why the Technocracy is successful as it is because they're a Weaver cult, just like how Pentex is wildly successful by aide and allegiance to the Wyrm. The only different between Pentex and the Technocracy is that Pentex is fully cognizant of being vassals to the Wyrm; while the Technocracy is unaware of the Weaver because the Weaver works subtly and through the low-whirring shifts of the OneSong.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's what the werewolves think. But <b>Mage</b> has <i>long</i> since moved past the point where <b>Werewolf</b> cosmology has anything more than a passing relevance to it. <br /> <br /> Stasis, Dynamism, and Entropy are distinct from, and arguably more fundamental than, the Triat: the Wyrm is the spiritual manifestation of Entropy; but unless your Focus is one that incorporates the notion that spirits are the fundamental building blocks of reality, you're probably not going to buy into the idea that the Wyrm <i>is</i> Entropy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433856#post1433856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Earthly Foundations are BS in Mage because any Mage that is Arete 7+ or above can completely wreck any notion of Earthly Foundations. The only reason why they don't do it is because with their high insight they already know the trivialities of the Ascension War and Earth itself.</div> </div> </div> </div> The fact that it takes Spheres in the 7+ range (assuming you accept <b>Masters of the Art</b>, which many of us, including Brucato, don't) to alter the likes of Earthly Foundations doesn't make them BS. Nobody has said that EFs can't be changed; only that it requires something more than merely changing the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T20:08:34-08:00","id":1433874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433865#post1433865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that it takes Spheres in the 7+ range (assuming you accept <b>Masters of the Art</b>, which many of us, including Brucato, don't) to alter the likes of Earthly Foundations doesn't make them BS. Nobody has said that EFs can't be changed; only that it requires something more than merely changing the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree<br /> <br /> But I have to say: The idea that Arete 7+ (that, btw, many Masters implied in the Ascencion War *do* have. It's not the province of Archmasters alone) can &quot;wreck any notion of Eartly Foundations&quot; it's not really supported by Mage books.<br /> <br /> Now, when people says Arete X they're usually implying Spheres at that level. So let's go into what MotA has to say: It's my understanding that Masters of the Art version of Archspheres not only doesn't imply you can change Earthly Foundations, it actually provides heavy *mechanical* reasons to think <i>even Spheres at 9 </i>can't &quot;wreck Eartly Foundations&quot; easily, if at all.<br /> <br /> The clearest example: Note that Forces 9 clearly states that any attempt at changing a cosmic force (like <b><i>gravity</i></b>, how curious, the de-facto Eartly Foundation sample in this thread) it's going to be <i>undone </i>in a matter of <i>seconds</i>. Who it's undoing this mega-Archmagick if not Foundations or the Consensus acting exactly as Foundations would?<br /> <br /> To add to that, Masters of the Art mentions Paradox being a big deal for Archspheres and Archmasters in general. There's a section in the books about that. Only Arch-Prime (that not all Archmasters have) can really deal with Paradox, and it's implied that because these spells are also inherently Vulgar, it's kind of a damocles sword. Oh, and by the fact that most Archmasters go hide in the Umbra, and do all sort of crazy shit (like shredding their own Avatars) to avoid Paradox<br /> <br /> Paradox it's reality pushing against your magick. If Archmasters were easily capable of &quot;wreck any notion of Eartly Foundations&quot; (<i>regardless if you understand them as beliefs deeply ingrained in the Consensus, or as an outside force with competing or superior power</i>), they shouldn't have so many problems with 'dox.<br /> <br /> I could get behind *Oracles* being able to &quot;wreck Eartly Foundations&quot; (but not doing so as part of their mysterious agendas) - perhaps. I could get behind Exemplars with Spheres at <b>10</b> being able to wreck the Foundations if they want (but they don't seem to want, perhaps because at that point they pretty much *represent* the Foundations, and migth be more inclined to preserve them that to make wild changes). Ascended Masters, sure they can (assuming Ascencion isn't a myth, and that the Ascended can and do affect our lesser reality)<br /> <br /> These three types of mages are also *trully* beyond the Ascencion War or mortal concerns. Ordinary Archamsters do get into the War from time to time<br /> (ehem...Porthos...ehem - Arete 9, by the way)<br /> <br /> Bottom line: Mere Arete 7+ most categorically *doesn't* allow one to fuck on the Consensus, much less on Cosmological Constants or Earthly Foundations (that are either <i>the Consensus</i>, or an even greater power), not even with MotA and a few Archsphere dots thrown into the mix.<br /> You need to look WAY above - it's, like, a ToJ Al-Aswad tier feat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-29-2021, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T21:58:58-08:00","id":1433882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mere Arete 7+ most categorically *doesn't* allow one to fuck on the Consensus,</div> </div> </div> </div>Bruh, a cabal of atleast 3 Arch-Masters with Mind 9 (One Mind) can easily change the Consensus just by influencing every mind on Earth in about 1 to 2 turns, even from the other side of the High Umbra. GG no Re. Actually if all the Arch-Masters in the oWoD universe got together to do something, they'd just flatly win the Ascension War over the Technocracy. They don't just do it because by that point their metaphysical form of thought has already past such things and they have entirely different Seekings that is entire above the Ascension War futility. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">only that it requires something more than merely changing the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that other factor is Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T08:43:32-08:00","id":1433930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mere Arete 7+ most categorically *doesn't* allow one to fuck on the Consensus...You need to look WAY above - it's, like, a ToJ Al-Aswad tier feat</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433882#post1433882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh, a cabal of atleast 3 Arch-Masters with Mind 9 (One Mind) can easily change the Consensus just by influencing every mind on Earth in about 1 to 2 turns, even from the other side of the High Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bruh, that requires A LOT more than your Arete 7+. Moving the goalposts much? Arch-Masters with Spheres at 9, if they exist, are on a similar level as powerful Exemplars and Oracles.<br /> <br /> Also, who cares if you do it from the other side of the High Umbra?, Paradox it's dependant on the place where an effect takes place, not where you're casting it. And trying to alter belief in Foundations in one or two seconds, would likely be quite Vulgar<br /> <br /> Still, one has to wonder: what if the effect it's to <i>alter the Consensus in such a way that the very Effect causing the alteration would be deemed Coincident</i>?. I'm tempted to put this as an example of why Foundations/Constants aren't dependant on the Consensus (otherwise Mind 9 can do Forces 9 better than Forces 9) - but &quot;Consensus is all&quot; defenders still have one card uppon their sleeves: Vulgarity it's determined <i>before the effect it's casted. </i>Hence, your alteration of the Consensus migth still be <i>very </i>Vulgar...IDK.<br /> <br /> But, hey, I grant you that you've managed to changed Foundations at &quot;only&quot; <b><i>level 9 </i></b>depending on how ST interprets Paradox working, and assuming Foundations don't come from a force distinct from the Consensus. If they come from an outside force (my personal cup of tea), then you've changed nothing<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually if all the Arch-Masters in the oWoD universe got together to do something, they'd just flatly win the Ascension War over the Technocracy. They don't just do it because by that point their metaphysical form of thought has already past such things and they have entirely different Seekings that is entire above the Ascension War futility. </div> </div> </div>I think you're conflating mere Archmasters with Oracles and similar. I'm starting to think you haven't read Masters of the Art.<br /> <br /> Because the Technocracy *has* Archmages, according to MotA (Arch-Scientists).<br /> <br /> Incidentaly, that's the reason given in MotA of why this doesn't happen: The escalation (and Paradox) that would be unleashed if Archmasters started to fight against Arch-Scientists would be catastrophical. Many, if not most, Archmasters aren't really *above* the Factions - they just don't get involved in the War very often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-30-2021, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T09:22:57-08:00","id":1433933,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a><br /> <br /> Also: &quot;Bruh, a cabal of atleast 3 Arch-Masters with Mind 9...&quot;<br /> <br /> XD<br /> <br /> Bruh, even Al-Aswad cabal of Anty-Oracles most likely doesn't have that much Mind (Al-Aswad himself having 8. I would think only the Mind Aswadim has more than that, since Al it's supposed to be vastly more powerful than the others).<br /> <br /> Think about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T13:53:07-08:00","id":1434035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433861#post1433861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The heck are the chaoticians?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once a cross-Convention Technocracy group, the Chaoticians (then known as the Probability Engineers) took the side of the Virtual Adepts during the 50s VA/NWO Cold War because the VA were the only Technocrats who took them seriously. Using their mastery of Entropy, they have predicted every recession since their foundation, including those recessions that occurred before the VA split from the Technocracy, (and warned the Syndicate, although the Syndicate <i>always</i> ignores them) and planned many of the Virtual Adept's most successful missions. The Chaoticians are also among the Adepts most ready to work with the rest of the Council, bonding with other Traditions over things like arcane mathematics, numerology, gematria, and the I Ching.<br /> <br /> Chaotician recruitment material (open to anyone who asks for it) has been known to deprogram Technocrats, leading some Adepts to believe that they're stuffing Mind magick in.<br /> <br /> Source:<br /> Tradition Book: Virtual Adepts (Revised)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","user":"JagneStormskull","date":".  Grammar correction. 02-01-2021, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T14:02:54-08:00","id":1434038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433882#post1433882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bruh, a cabal of atleast 3 Arch-Masters with Mind 9 (One Mind)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that all it would take to execute your plan? Because I'm not sure there are that many Mind 9 Arch-Masters in history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T05:09:14-08:00","id":1434108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1426997-when-was-the-exact-moment-that-the-technocratcy-began-to-be-written-as-less-evil?p=1433930#post1433930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, one has to wonder: what if the effect it's to <i>alter the Consensus in such a way that the very Effect causing the alteration would be deemed Coincident</i>?. I'm tempted to put this as an example of why Foundations/Constants aren't dependant on the Consensus (otherwise Mind 9 can do Forces 9 better than Forces 9) - but &quot;Consensus is all&quot; defenders still have one card uppon their sleeves: Vulgarity it's determined <i>before the effect it's casted. </i>Hence, your alteration of the Consensus migth still be <i>very </i>Vulgar...IDK.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would be extremely Vulgar, if it could even happen. There's another card I'd play as well, though, which is that simple mind control doesn't change the consensus like that. <br /> <br /> To really make this work, everyone one earth would have to be hollowed out to the level of a newborn baby, so that even their earliest beliefs were eliminated. Then after you spiritually lobotomized them they would need to be built up from scratch, given new identities and experiences that reinforce the new beliefs. Also, since there is a lot of indication that the High Umbra and the Consensus are intertwined, you'd have to scrub the High Umbra clean as well to prevent it from contaminating your new consensus.<br /> <br /> This is not a simple thing a couple of Masters could do while having a few beers. This is a complicated Ascension level event.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}